{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DtxJEsLC8ka3FgiAvpqGo3","type":"tool_result","content":"   647 docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md\n   313 docs/ANIMATION_STUDIO.md\n   170 docs/ASSET_IMPORT.md\n   168 docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md\n   145 docs/ASSET_STUDIO_LIVE.md\n  1527 docs/ASSET_SYSTEM_PLAN.md\n   652 docs/COOP_PLAN.md\n   420 docs/CREATURE_STUDIO.md\n   219 docs/DESIGN.md\n    64 docs/DOCTRINE.md\n   166 docs/ESCALATIONS.md\n    73 docs/FEEDBACK.md\n   170 docs/GAME.md\n  3881 docs/HISTORY.md\n   185 docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md\n   122 docs/MATERIALS.md\n    59 docs/PROGRESS.md\n   381 docs/REFERENCE.md\n  9362 total\n1:# Reference\n12:## Code map\n114:## Studios\n164:## Tools\n270:## Browser and phones\n280:## Controls\n316:## Tests\n\n8:- [Browser and phones](#browser-and-phones): running the web build headless, emulating a phone.\n9-- [Controls](#controls): keyboard, gamepad, touch and the fixed system keys.\n10-- [Tests](#tests): what each suite covers.\n11-\n12-## Code map\n13-```\n14-crates/\n15-  pav_core    simulation, no window/GPU/audio deps: Sim, entities, physics (rapier3d),\n16-              static regions (statics.rs: terrain chunks, rooms, hub; active or dormant;\n17-              blocks, decor and baked library props: drawn by the view's region cache, one\n18-              collider box each, no entity),\n19-              world.rs (pavilion layout, streaming, room tracking), room.rs (room files),\n20-              terrain.rs (procedural wilderness), tile levels (level.rs), characters\n21-              (character.rs: movement models instant/momentum/grid/committed, jump,\n22-              crouch/crawl, ladders, ledge grab/mantle, swimming, axis lock, moving platforms,\n23-              knockback, pushing shares momentum, bombs, ice slide), puppet (puppet.rs: body\n24-              plans biped/spider/lizard/beetle/blob/quadruped, procedural animation, hit recoil,\n25-              creature lunges, foot IK, legs that stride the way the body travels, idle breathing\n26-              and blinks, cutout look and camera cheats; the biped is a `Skel` of joints that the\n27-              procedural animation, moves and clips each produce and `dress` turns into parts),\n28-              moves.rs (attacks and gestures as data, anim/moves.toml: arcs around the shoulders,\n29-              wind-up from wherever the hands were, strikes with lunge/lean/twist/hop/spin,\n30-              follow-through; skills name a move, a look may name its own per skill and combo\n31-              swing: `attack_moves`), clips.rs (motion clips: readable key poses\n32-              translated from open animation libraries, retargeted onto the biped with IK,\n33-              crossfaded over the procedural animation, upper body only or mirrored; performers,\n34-              idle clips, walk clips played as fast as the character moves), anim.rs (the /anim files: embedded, live reload), rig.rs (creature feet that plant and step,\n35-              follow-the-leader spines, verlet tails/antennae), ai.rs (NPC brains: idle,\n36-              wander, patrol, circle, follow; they drive characters through InputFrames),\n37-              nav.rs (walkable grid from blocks and props, A* paths, flow fields),\n38-              games/ (the hook a new game implements, `Game`, and `GAMES`, the list that\n39-              makes each one a scene; starter.rs + starter.toml, the template:\n40-              docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md),\n41-              fxdef.rs (object lights / particle emitters / distortion, view-only),\n42-              vehicle.rs (drift car on rapier's raycast vehicle, arcade helicopter: flight only,\n43-              no weapons, damage or fuel), health.rs (shootable rapier objects: hp, score, boss\n44-              phases/bar, finish),\n45-              stealth.rs (guard sight cones with line of sight and an alert meter),\n46-              zones.rs (trigger zones + labels), course.rs (timers, gates, checkpoints, pits,\n47-              pads, camera cues, hits/respawn), behaviors.rs (movers, rotators, emitters,\n48-              spawners), projectile.rs (lightweight bullets), feel.rs (feel metrics),\n--\n270:## Browser and phones\n271-Headless Chromium can run the browser build (WebGPU on SwiftShader): launch with\n272-`--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`\n273-(other flag sets show a blank canvas). `?room=NAME&seed=N` picks the start room.\n274-Phones: emulate one in headless Chromium with Playwright (`viewport 844x390, isMobile, hasTouch,\n275-deviceScaleFactor: 1`; Chrome's DPR emulation leaves the canvas at CSS size) and drive it with\n276-CDP `Input.dispatchTouchEvent`; SwiftShader frames take about a second, so send a tap's start and\n277-end back to back.\n278-From WSL2 you can launch the Windows build directly: `./target/x86_64-pc-windows-gnu/dist/shardfall.exe`.\n279-\n280-## Controls\n281-Keyboard+mouse: WASD move, Space jump (hold = higher), C/Ctrl crouch, Z crawl toggle, F or left\n282-click throw bomb at the cursor, Shift walk slowly, walk into ladders to climb, jump at a ledge\n283-and keep pushing toward it to grab it (push again/Space = pull up, C = drop), Space/C swim up/down,\n284-committed model: C while running = dodge roll; right-drag rotate camera, wheel zoom, 1–8 camera\n285-presets. Gamepad: left stick move, right stick aim, A jump,\n286-B crouch, Y crawl, X/RT bomb, LT slow, LB/RB rotate camera, D-pad zoom, Start menu, Back rewind.\n287-\n288-Shardfall: WASD move, LMB/RMB/Q/E/R/F skills, Space dodge, 1 potion, Shift attack in place,\n289-G use (vendor, stash, portal, gambler, alchemist, the way down, cursed chests), I/Tab\n290-inventory, P passive tree, C character, K skills, M map, T town portal; gamepad\n291-X/Y/B/RB/LB/RT skills, A dodge, D-pad up potion, D-pad right use, D-pad left map, D-pad down\n292-panels (LB/RB switch); in any window or the menu the stick drives a cursor (A click, X\n293-right-click, hold Y shift, right stick scroll, B close). Controller flows can be scripted and\n294-screenshotted: `shardfall --pad-script FILE` (lines `<frames> [left=x,y] [right=x,y]\n295-[hold=A,Y] [tap=DPadDown]`, see `PadScript` in input.rs).\n296-\n297-Touch (phones, tablets; the browser build): put a thumb down anywhere and drag to move (an\n298-invisible stick); attacks are automatic (the nearest foe in reach; a menu setting); the fan in\n299-the bottom right: dodge (big button), skills (tap: at the nearest foe · drag: aim, let go to\n300-cast, back onto the button to cancel · hold: keep casting), potion, and a \"use\" button that\n301-appears when something is in reach; top right: menu and bag. Swipe messages, banners and the\n302-minimap away; tap the minimap for the big map; tap the game outside a window to close it.\n303-Graphics quality (Auto/Low/Medium/High) and auto-attack are in the touch pause menu.\n304-\n305-H (world demo): how the room you are in works (the station guide: steps, pads, live settings,\n306-uses, ask-for-it phrases, cost, the engine's code, words); outside rooms the field guide\n307-(guide_ui.rs). Stepping on a pad with a note shows the note at the bottom for a while.\n308-Fixed system layer (never rebinds): Esc pause menu · F1 tuning panel · F2 rooms (teleport) ·\n309-F3 boot diagnostics · F4 leave room · F5 reset room · F6 pause · F7 step · F8/F9 slower/faster ·\n310-F10 edit mode (sandbox) · hold Backspace rewind · F11 fullscreen · F12 screenshot.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"501e7141-3737-4a8e-9cac-eb3584714d8d","uuid":"59680b22-6d22-4608-aa1f-1eab463e6559","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:15.750Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"   647 docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md\n   313 docs/ANIMATION_STUDIO.md\n   170 docs/ASSET_IMPORT.md\n   168 docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md\n   145 docs/ASSET_STUDIO_LIVE.md\n  1527 docs/ASSET_SYSTEM_PLAN.md\n   652 docs/COOP_PLAN.md\n   420 docs/CREATURE_STUDIO.md\n   219 docs/DESIGN.md\n    64 docs/DOC