t/hop/spin,\n30-              follow-through; skills name a move, a look may name its own per skill and combo\n31-              swing: `attack_moves`), clips.rs (motion clips: readable key poses\n32-              translated from open animation libraries, retargeted onto the biped with IK,\n33-              crossfaded over the procedural animation, upper body only or mirrored; performers,\n34-              idle clips, walk clips played as fast as the character moves), anim.rs (the /anim files: embedded, live reload), rig.rs (creature feet that plant and step,\n35-              follow-the-leader spines, verlet tails/antennae), ai.rs (NPC brains: idle,\n36-              wander, patrol, circle, follow; they drive characters through InputFrames),\n37-              nav.rs (walkable grid from blocks and props, A* paths, flow fields),\n38-              games/ (the hook a new game implements, `Game`, and `GAMES`, the list that\n39-              makes each one a scene; starter.rs + starter.toml, the template:\n40-              docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md),\n41-              fxdef.rs (object lights / particle emitters / distortion, view-only),\n42-              vehicle.rs (drift car on rapier's raycast vehicle, arcade helicopter: flight only,\n43-              no weapons, damage or fuel), health.rs (shootable rapier objects: hp, score, boss\n44-              phases/bar, finish),\n45-              stealth.rs (guard sight cones with line of sight and an alert meter),\n46-              zones.rs (trigger zones + labels), course.rs (timers, gates, checkpoints, pits,\n47-              pads, camera cues, hits/respawn), behaviors.rs (movers, rotators, emitters,\n48-              spawners), projectile.rs (lightweight bullets), feel.rs (feel metrics),\n--\n270:## Browser and phones\n271-Headless Chromium can run the browser build (WebGPU on SwiftShader): launch with\n272-`--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`\n273-(other flag sets show