ppet performs, as numbers instead of code.\n# A skill names one (`anim = \"overhead\"` in game/skills.toml); townsfolk and tools use them too.\n# Edit, then `anim_reload` in the REPL (or the running game) and `animsheet move=NAME` to look.\n#\n# How a move plays. Its progress runs 0..1 over the skill's own time, and the hit lands where the\n# skill says; the move's three phases are stretched to fit around that moment:\n#   wind     anticipation: the hand travels from wherever it was (the walk, or the last move's\n#            end: chained attacks never snap) to the start of the arc; the body coils back.\n#   active   the strike: the hand sweeps the arc from `from` to `to` (degrees) at `reach`, the\n#            body lunges, leans, twists with the swing and may hop or spin.\n#   recover  holds the end pose (`hold` of it), follows through a little, then eases back.\n#   hit      the share of `active` where it connects (the skill's hit moment lines up with it).\n#\n# Fields (defaults in brackets):\n#   name, about   what it is called and what it looks like (a model picks moves by `about`)\n#   hand          right | left | both (two-handed grip) | pair (both hands, mirrored) | kick (the\n#                 right foot)                                                        [right]\n#   plane         ground: a level arc around the shoulders (0 = straight ahead, + = the right side);\n#                 side: an up-and-down arc in front (0 = straight ahead, + = up)     [ground]\n#   from, to      degrees along the arc                                              [0, 0]\n#   height        [start, end] above the shoulders, in arm lengths (ground plane); kicks: shares of\n#                 hip height above the ground                                        [-0.76]\n#   reach         arm lengths from the shoulders (kicks: leg lengths); [start, end] extends a thrust\n#                                                                                    [0.82]\n#   wind, active, recover   seconds: the move's shape (the skill decides the real time)\n#                                                                         [0.06, 0.10, 0.18]\n#   hold          share of the recovery spent holding the end pose                   [0.3]\n#   lunge, hop    metres the body steps into the strike and jumps (on a 1.8 m figure) [0.064, 0]\n#   crouch        0..1 dip                                                           [0.15]\n#   lean          radians forward lean through the strike (negative leans back)      [0.3]\n#   twist         how much the torso turns with the swing angle                      [1]\n#   spin          the whole body turns once during the strike                        [false]\n#   trail         the held weapon draws a swing trail                                [true]\n#   alt           the move played on alternate swings (a slash answered by a backslash)\n#\n# The first nine are the engine's original actions, in their original order.\n\n[[move]]\nname = \"slash\"\nabout = \"a level sword swing from the right shoulder across to the left; alternate swings come back as a backslash\"\nfrom = 97\nto = -97\nheight = [-0.65, -0.98]\nwind = 0.08\nactive = 0.1\nrecover = 0.22\nalt = \"backslash\"\n\n[[move]]\nname = \"overhead\"\nabout = \"the blade raised high behind the head and chopped straight down in front, crouching into it\"\nplane = \"side\"\nfrom = 138\nto = -72\nreach = 0.76\nwind = 0.16\nactive = 0.09\nrecover = 0.26\nlunge = 0.106\ncrouch = 0.35\n31\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]\n[[move]]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RtxUFCNtpSE8fNRUAudASK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
