{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H7cJZkb2BD828PtbhVBz5L","type":"tool_result","content":"370 ../probe/hub-check.mjs\n34: * nothing with WebGL or a 2D canvas instead. --browser-args passes flags to\n37: *   --browser-args \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader\"\n48: *                                    [--retrofit [--original <path>]] [--draws-only] [--record] [--browser-args \"<flags>\"]\n66:const args = process.argv.slice(2);\n68:  const at = args.indexOf(`--${name}`);\n70:  const [value] = args.splice(at, 2).slice(1);\n76:const asJson = args.includes('--json');\n77:const solo = !args.includes('--no-solo');\n78:const retrofit = args.includes('--retrofit');\n79:const drawsOnly = args.includes('--draws-only');\n80:const record = args.includes('--record');\n82:const browserArgs = (option('browser-args', '') || '').split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\n84:const games = args.filter((a) => !a.startsWith('--')).map(asPath);\n174:const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH, args: ['--no-sandbox', '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required', ...browserArgs] });\n180:      runs.push({ game, players: 1, scenario: 'draws', pass: report.pass, checks: report.checks });\n186:      runs.push({ game, players: 0, scenario: 'static', pass: client.pass, checks: [client] });\n192:    const plan = retrofit && !asked ? [] : counts.map((n) => ({ n, scenario: 'standard' }));\n194:    if (asked || leaving <= seats[1]) plan.push({ n: leaving, scenario: 'host-leave' });\n196:    if (!retrofit && mode && !SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode) && (asked || (seats[0] <= 2 && seats[1] >= 2))) plan.push({ n: 2, scenario: 'server' });\n197:    for (const { n, scenario } of plan) {\n205:      const query = { game, players: n, latency: 150, jitter: 50, loss: 5, auto: 1, scenario, play: 8000 };\n210:      const finished = await page.waitForSelector('body[data-complete=\"true\"]', { timeout: PAGE_MS }).then(() => true, () => false);\n222:      runs.push({ game, players: n, scenario, pass: report.pass, checks: report.checks });\n224:        console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  ${n} players  ${scenario}`);\n231:      runs.push({ game, players: 1, scenario: 'alone', pass: report.pass, checks: report.checks });\n347:    const mine = runs.filter((r) => r.game === game && r.scenario !== 'server');\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n/**\n * hub-check.mjs — does a game keep the AI Hub Session Protocol?\n *\n * Runs lib/hub/harness.html?auto=1 against each game, at the player counts its\n * hub:session-players allows: hello, ready under the hub's card with no key\n * press, the start, traffic, a player leaving, time-up and a valid result. Then\n * once more with the host leaving. Then the game on its own, outside a session:\n * it opens, Enter and Space are pressed, and it must draw its screen with no\n * errors, the session client inactive and Math.random left alone. Before any\n * game script runs, every frame in session mode gets alert, confirm, prompt,\n * window.open and socket constructors wrapped, so calling them is caught.\n * Needs Playwright, which is not a dependency (see shots.mjs).\n *\n * Parallel is played at 1 and 2 players: nothing is shared, so more copies\n * prove nothing more. Its checks expect Math.random seeded the same on every\n * copy, progress from every copy, and no game traffic.\n *\n * Ghost and shared world are played at 2, 3 and 4 players on a poor network\n * (150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss). Ghost is checked like parallel, except that every\n * copy sends its player. A shared world wants traffic both ways, and is\n * played once more at 2 players with its world hosted by one more copy that\n * has no player of its own, as a dedicated server would host it (README,\n * \"Shared world\"). That run is reported like any; --record does not hold it\n * against a game, since no server runs yet.\n *\n * --retrofit is for an existing game upgraded to parallel: it is played once,\n * at 2 players with one of them leaving. With --original <path>, errors the\n * original page already had are forgiven when it is opened on its own.\n * --draws-only does only that last part, for any page: the retrofit runs it on","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"501e7141-3737-4a8e-9cac-eb3584714d8d","uuid":"bea4a311-6bfe-4620-ac5f-a9e7f16a5429","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:42:27.588Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"370 ../probe/hub-check.mjs\n34: * nothing with WebGL or a 2D canvas instead. --browser-args passes flags to\n37: *   --browser-args \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader\"\n48: *                                    [--retrofit [--original <path>]] [--draws-only] [--record] [--browser-args \"<flags>\"]\n66:const args = process.argv.slice(2);\n68:  const at = args.indexOf(`--${name}`);\n70:  const [value] = args.splice(at, 2).slice(1);\n76:const asJson = args.includes('--json');\n77:const solo = !args.includes('--no-solo');\n78:const retrofit = args.includes('--retrofit');\n79:const drawsOnly = args.includes('--draws-only');\n80:const record = args.includes('--record');\n82:const browserArgs = (option('browser-args', '') || '').split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\n84:const games = args.filter((a) => !a.startsWith('--')).map(asPath);\n174:const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH, args: ['--no-sandbox', '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required', ...browserArgs] });\n180:      runs.push({ game, players: 1, scenario: 'draws', pass: report.pass, checks: report.checks });\n186:      runs.push({ game, players: 0, scenario: 'static', pass: client.pass, checks: [client] });\n192:    const plan = retrofit && !asked ? [] : counts.map((n) => ({ n, scenario: 'standard' }));\n194:    if (asked || leaving <= seats[1]) plan.push({ n: leaving, scenario: 'host-leave' });\n196:    if (!retrofit && mode && !SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode) && (asked || (seats[0] <= 2 && seats[1] >= 2))) plan.push({ n: 2, scenario: 'server' });\n197:    for (const { n, scenario } of plan) {\n205:      const query = { game, players: n, latency: 150, jitter: 50, loss: 5, auto: 1, scenario, play: 8000 };\n210:      const finished = await page.waitForSelector('body[data-complete=\"true\"]', { timeout: PAGE_MS }).then(() => true, () => false);\n222:      runs.push({ game, players: n, scenario, pass: report.pass, checks: report.checks });\n224:        console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  ${n} players  ${scenario}`);\n231:      runs.push({ game, players: 1, scenario: 'alone', pass: report.pass, checks: report.checks });\n347:    const mine = runs.filter((r) => r.game === game && r.scenario !== 'server');\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n/**\n * hub-check.mjs — does a game keep the AI Hub Session Protocol?\n *\n * Runs lib/hub/harness.html?auto=1 against each game, at the player counts its\n * hub:session-players allows: hello, ready under the hub's card with no key\n * press, the start, traffic, a player leaving, time-up and a valid result. Then\n * once more with the host leaving. Then the game on its own, outside a session:\n * it opens, Enter and Space are pressed, and it must draw its screen with no\n * errors, the session client inactive and Math.random left alone. Before any\n * game script runs, every frame in session mode gets alert, confirm, prompt,\n * window.open and socket constructors wrapped, so calling them is caught.\n * Needs Playwright, which is not a dependency (see shots.mjs).\n *\n * Parallel is played at 1 and 2 players: nothing is shared, so more copies\n * prove nothing more. Its checks expect Math.random seeded the same on every\n * copy, progress from every copy, and no game traffic.\n *\n * Ghost and shared world are played at 2, 3 and 4 players on a poor network\n * (150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss). Ghost is checked like parallel, except that every\n * copy sends its player. A shared world wants traffic both ways, and is\n * played once more at 2 players with its world hosted by one more copy that\n * has no player of its own, as a dedicated server would host it (README,\n * \"Shared world\"). That run is reported like any; --record does not hold it\n * against a game, since no server runs yet.\n *\n * --retrofit is for an existing game upgraded to parallel: it is played once,\n * at 2 players with one of them leaving. With --original <path>, errors the\n * original page already had are forgiven when it is opened on its own.\n * --draws-only does only that last part, for any page: the retrofit runs it on","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01H7cJZkb2BD828PtbhVBz5L","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
