{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCujQu4i5vMAd2RBZfM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CfNW7TES1aoDTbzAeT9kf4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211956__x710a06/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b) if count==0 else s.replace(a,b,count)\n\nrep('''git clone https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall.git engine && git -C engine checkout 49ef2ba\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js   # into tools/hub/, with harness.html, bridge.js, round.js\n''','''git clone https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall.git engine && git -C engine checkout 49ef2ba\nmkdir -p tools/hub && for f in README.md session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js; do\n  curl -fsS -o tools/hub/$f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done\n''')\nrep('''- Native sim speed is about 21,000 ticks/s, so a scripted run through the whole game takes under a few minutes.\n''','''- Native sim speed was about 21,000 ticks/s in a test room with 17 entities and no AI. Expect less with crowds, but still far above real time, so a scripted run through the whole game stays practical.\n''')\nrep('''**Software rendering is slow [V]:** about 1.5 fps at 1280×720, about 5 fps at 640×360. The sim catches up at most 8 ticks per frame (`simhost.rs`), so a browser runs at 10 to 40 ticks/s.''','''**Software rendering is slow [V]:** about 1.5 fps at 1280×720 and 5 fps at 640×360 with the bare starter, and 2 to 3 fps at 640×360 with a dressed harbor scene. The sim catches up at most 8 ticks per frame (`simhost.rs`), so a browser runs at 10 to 40 ticks/s against the real 60.''')\nrep('''- KayKit figures are chibi-proportioned [V]. Don't use them for people in this game.\n''','''- KayKit figures are chibi-proportioned [V]. Don't use them for people in this game.\n- Puppets default to `eyes_to_camera = 0.6`, a cheat for high cameras that slides the eyes toward the viewer. Set it to 0 on every look: this camera sits behind the head.\n''')\nrep('''- The hub owns Create + Options held together: ignore Options while Create is held.\n''','''- ✕ does the prompted action on press. With no prompt showing, holding it runs.\n- The hub owns Create + Options held together: ignore Options while Create is held.\n''')\nrep('''list: Continue, New Claim, Chapters, Claims Rush, Settings, About.''','''list: Continue (if a save exists), New Claim, Chapters (after finishing the game once), Claims Rush, Settings, About.''')\nrep('''There are 5 lamps across the game, plus a Ch5 lamp.''','''There are 6 lamps: Net Lane, Loading Dock, Halfway Hut, the Cliff Road hut, lighthouse floor 2, and the Quay before the Underwriter.''')\nrep('''Keep areas at or below 90×70 m: fog at 46 m hides the edges.''','''Keep areas within about 110 m on a side: fog at 46 m hides the edges.''')\nrep('''(the same bot code as §17)''','''(the same bot code as §16.4)''')\nrep('''which is what makes the whole game testable at 20,000 ticks/s.''','''which is what makes the whole game testable far faster than real time.''')\nrep('''(with `grip` and `tip` sockets, `kind = \"wand\"` works for holding [V])''','''(with `grip` and `tip` sockets; `weapon = { kind = \"wand\", asset = ... }` loads and draws [V], but the aim pose hid it in the test, so check its orientation early)''')\nrep('''cottages ×3 ([V] walls, wedge roof, lit windows with `emissive` ≤ what you want as a lamp)''','''cottages ×3 ([V] box walls, wedge roof, `emissive: 3` windows that glow and light the street)''')\nrep('''Pell at a desk, tiny and immaculate, the manifest in front of Mrs. Vane. The cold open of the climax: he's a puppet, and his jaw opens further than it should. Mrs. Vane signs with a flourish.''','''Pell at a desk, tiny and immaculate, the manifest in front of Mrs. Vane. He's been a puppet all along, and his jaw opens further than it should. Mrs. Vane signs with a flourish.''')\ns=s.replace('Harbour','Harbor')\nrep('''**Engine feedback notes:** keep a short running list as you go, since your TASK.md asks what you changed and where you got stuck. §14.1 is most of it.\n''','''**Engine feedback notes:** keep a short running list as you go, since your TASK.md asks what you changed and where you got stuck. §14.1 is most of it.\n\n**Final reply:** put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply as well as on the About screen. Further research is your choice. Report what you actually did, adding that this plan's research covered the engine source and the hub protocol.\n''')\nrep('''- In a session: no pause (Options opens only volume settings), no quit, restart or storage writes, no `alert`, no sockets.\n''','''- In a session: no pause (Options opens only volume settings), no quit, restart or storage writes, no `alert`, no sockets. If `navigator.gpu` is missing, call `AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU')`.\n''')\nrep('''`pointerlockchange` losing lock in play → pause). Stick to `look`. Native builds use winit''','''`pointerlockchange` losing lock in play → pause). `movementX/Y` works before the lock too, so looking never depends on it. Stick to `look`. Native builds use winit''')\nrep('''mouse hover moves focus; click activates. In play, stick changes look and position.\n''','''mouse hover moves focus; click activates. In play, stick changes look and position; left-click on a highlighted world object interacts.\n''')\nrep('''Hook additions (all default-implemented; `starter` keeps working):\n''','''Hook additions (all default-implemented so `starter` keeps working; add each to `DynGame` and `GameBox` like the existing methods):\n''')\nrep('''With the full set, the unmodified engine plus a JS stand-in for game logic **passed** the harness at 2 players, 3 and 4 players on `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&play=8000`, 4 with `scenario=host-leave`, and 2 with `scenario=server`. Each run took 10 to 20 s, and `ready()` fired within 2 s of load.''','''With the full set, the engine's starter plus a JS stand-in for game logic **passed** the harness on `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&play=8000` at 2, 3 and 4 players, at 4 with `scenario=host-leave`, and at 2 with `scenario=server`. Each run took 10 to 20 s, and `ready()` fired within 2 s of load.''')\n# bot section\nrep('''### 16.3 Data-driven content (the designer tools)''','''### 16.3 Data-driven content (the designer tools)''')\nrep('''---\n\n## 17. Testing\n''','''### 16.4 The bot\nOne bot serves the whole-game test, attract mode and Claims Rush AI temps. It plays through the same `InputFrame`s and `GameCmd`s a player uses.\n- **Goals come from data:** each chapter lists its beats in order in `chapters.toml`, each with a bot goal: `go_to(marker)`, `interact(id)`, `clear(encounter)`, `hold(seconds)`, `buy(item)`, `tune(weapon, track)`, `fit_pickup`, `save`, `command_vane(wait|follow)`, `qte`, `boss(script)`.\n- **Fighting:** pick the nearest threat, set `look` toward its head by the shortest turn, hold aim, fire within 1.5°. Press ✕ when a follow-up prompt shows, reload at empty, heal under 40% HP, sidestep when a telegraph is close, switch weapon by range.\n- **Moving:** path on the nav grids with `nav_link`s for ladders and stairs. Teleport-if-stuck is allowed only with the attract cheats on.\n- **Bosses:** each has a small authored script (lure, expose, shoot the weak point).\n\nTeach the bot each rule as you add it, as the engine's guide says. A chapter isn't finished until the bot can finish it.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Testing\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"Harbour\\|TODO\\|xxx\" PLAN.md | head; wc -w PLAN.md; grep -n \"GameTitle\\|exit-interview\\|claude-opus\" PLAN.md | head","description":"Apply review fixes to PLAN.md and check banned names"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9808,"cache_read_input_tokens":549372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9808},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"501e7141-3737-4a8e-9cac-eb3584714d8d","uuid":"b1d94a60-7e4b-47eb-9827-873aee9a177d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:11:32.558Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCuj7HcVqcVxRGwsEBL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CfNW7TES1aoDTbzAeT9kf4":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211956__x710a06/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b) if count==0 else s.replace(a,b,count)\n\nrep('''git clone https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall.git engine && git -C engine checkout 49ef2ba\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js   # into tools/hub/, with harness.html, bridge.js, round.js\n''','''git clone https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall.git engine && git -C engine checkout 49ef2ba\nmkdir -p tools/hub && for f in README.md session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js; do\n  curl -fsS -o tools/hub/$f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done\n''')\nrep('''- Native sim speed is about 21,000 ticks/s, so a scripted run through the whole game takes under a few minutes.\n''','''- Native sim speed was about 21,000 ticks/s in a test room with 17 entities and no AI. Expect less with crowds, but still far above real time, so a scripted run through the whole game stays practical.\n''')\nrep('''**Software rendering is slow [V]:** about 1.5 fps at 1280×720, about 5 fps at 640×360. The sim catches up at most 8