{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCxM35Vt6nyLQ9gxEoF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013rpyb18sHXDnkqxbL3zfqk","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211956__x710a06/work/PLAN.md","offset":330,"limit":330},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13484,"cache_read_input_tokens":563369,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13484},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"501e7141-3737-4a8e-9cac-eb3584714d8d","uuid":"eb8ba63d-e6ac-4bc9-b034-37b01b84a974","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:11:44.652Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCxLhVH3tvuYZjrSjTr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013rpyb18sHXDnkqxbL3zfqk":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211956__x710a06/work/PLAN.md","offset":330,"limit":330}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013rpyb18sHXDnkqxbL3zfqk","type":"tool_result","content":"330\t### Chapter 3: Turning Tide (`causeway` 110×24 m and `crypt` 40×40 m, overcast dusk, rain, about 13 min)\n331\t1. **The Causeway.** A stone spit with cover stops. The tide rises in visible steps: flooded sections slow you (×0.7) and then knock you back to the last stop if you stay. Mrs. Vane walks at 3.0 m/s and must be told Wait or Follow (§8). Parishioners rise from the water and try to **carry Mrs. Vane off** (leg shot drops her). Hounds on sandbars. Tinners in rowboats (shoot the boat's lamp).\n332\t   - She gives Cass the **Flare Pistol** after the second attack: \"I'm not supposed to have that. Neither are you.\"\n333\t2. **Halfway Hut.** Blue lamp and radio. Teach the crate: \"Get in the crate, Mrs. Vane.\" \"I will not.\" She does.\n334\t3. **Chapel Yard.** Hold position while she works the sluice wheel (90 s). Co-op puzzle: two winches, one for each, cranked together to lift the crypt gate.\n335\t4. **St. Orran's Crypt.** Boss: **The Bell-Hermit**. Mrs. Vane stays above and shouts insults.\n336\t5. **Reward.** The Harpoon Gun on a saint's tomb. Tunnels under the rock lead to the cliffs. Chapter report.\n337\t\n338\t### Chapter 4: The Long Drop (`cliffs`, 100×45 m, storm, about 10 min). First to cut, see §18.\n339\t1. **Cliff Road.** Bailiffs appear. Seal Rifle in a hunter's hut. Scuttlers. Gulls scatter.\n340\t2. **Overwatch.** Cass on a ledge with the rifle while Mrs. Vane crosses a rope bridge (`style = \"bridge\"` chain) 60 m away, enemies at both ends. She fires flares at anything you miss. The bridge burns after she's over; Cass crosses at the run with a QTE.\n341\t3. **The Funicular.** A 60 s scripted ride down the cliff on a moving platform. Enemies leap on, you shoot the rope brake on the other car to stop it colliding, shoot falling cargo, QTE at the end when the cable snaps (L1 + R1 together).\n342\t4. **Lighthouse Gate.** Bailiffs drag Mrs. Vane inside as the gate drops: \"Keep your hands off the fur!\" Chapter report.\n343\t\n344\t### Chapter 5: The Underwriter (`lighthouse`, 30×30 m, 4 floors; then `quay` reused at storm night, flooded, about 13 min)\n345\t1. **Lighthouse climb.** Spiral stairs and ladders, floors link by ladders enemies also use. Bailiffs, Rooted, Flenser returns on floor 3 (fight it on a narrow gallery, shoot the rail to drop it into the sea). Blue lamp on floor 2.\n346\t2. **Lamp Room.** Pell at a desk, tiny and immaculate, the manifest in front of Mrs. Vane. He's been a puppet all along, and his jaw opens further than it should. Mrs. Vane signs with a flourish. \"That's not my signature, you little man. That's a cancellation.\" Saltroot erupts from Pell, the sea below lifts: **the Underwriter** rises in the harbor.\n347\t3. **Boss, flooded Quay.** The same streets as Ch1, knee-deep, at night, with the storm and lighthouse beam overhead. The Square's tannoys now play only breathing.\n348\t   - *Phase 1:* 6 glowing bulbs on tendrils around the square, each 400 HP. Tendrils sweep (dodge) and spawn Rooted.\n349\t   - *Phase 2:* the mouth rises at the wharf. Mrs. Vane, on the radio from the lamp room, swings the beam: while it's on the mouth, the mouth flinches open for 8 s. Fetch a charge from one of 4 crate stacks, carry it (no firing) to the **Whaling Cannon** on the wharf, load (✕), aim, fire down the throat. Three charges. Waves keep coming.\n350\t   - *Phase 3:* last charge is a QTE and the one-liner: **\"Claim denied.\"**\n351\t4. **Escape.** A 60 s timed run from the wharf to the pier through collapsing streets; Bram's boat, Mrs. Vane already aboard, complaining.\n352\t5. **Epilogue.** Radio. \"Harrow. Did you get a signature?\" Credits, Claim Settlement.\n353\t\n354\tThe last chapter in `chapters.toml` triggers ending and credits, so the ending stays valid if Ch4 is cut.\n355\t\n356\t---\n357\t\n358\t## 8. Mrs. Vane (escort)\n359\t\n360\t- 74 years old, 70 HP (shown top-left with her portrait). Walks at 3.0 m/s, at most 7 m behind Cass, on a flow field to Cass's feet. Never blocks a door or narrow lane: she steps aside when Cass walks into her.\n361\t- **Follow or Wait** on D-pad down or C. On Wait she stands, or, if a **lobster crate** is within 8 m, gets in it and can't be hit. A bubble icon marks her.\n362\t- **Enemies don't try to kill her, they carry her off:** a Parishioner with a free slot walks up, lifts her (`Walk_Carry`) and heads for the nearest exit marker. Reaching it is **game over** (\"The Harbormaster has received your client.\"). Any hit on the carrier drops her. Enemies also swing at her, 8 dmg. At 0 HP she's down for 20 s and must be helped up (✕), or the policy lapses.\n363\t- She hits anything adjacent with her handbag: 4 dmg + short stun, every 2.5 s. From Ch3, a flare every 20 s at the nearest enemy over 6 m away, which also tells players where trouble is.\n364\t- Your laser never harms her. Bullets stop on her with a flinch and a line (\"Do mind.\") but no damage, so she's never a tax on aim. Only explosions hurt her.\n365\t- She reacts to low cash, big kills, and treasures with dry lines. Her lines are a big part of the game's charm: don't leave her silent.\n366\t\n367\t---\n368\t\n369\t## 9. Interactions and QTEs\n370\t\n371\t**World interactions** (all data-driven in level TOML, each with a prompt):\n372\t- **Doors:** open slowly; pressing ✕ again kicks it open and knocks down anything behind.\n373\t- **Ladders:** climb; kick a ladder down when an enemy is on it.\n374\t- **Windows:** vault (0.8 s, invulnerable).\n375\t- **Dressers and shelves:** push (hold).\n376\t- **Rope:** shoot it to drop the load.\n377\t- **Crates, barrels, lobster pots:** knife or shot breaks and drops loot.\n378\t- **Oil barrels:** explode (3.5 m, 60 dmg, chain).\n379\t- **Hanging lanterns:** shoot to start a 2 m fire.\n380\t- **Valves:** steam.\n381\t- **Winches and wheels:** hold.\n382\t- **Fuses:** Key Item use.\n383\t- **Radio:** save.\n384\t- **Lamp:** trader.\n385\t- **Notes:** read.\n386\t\n387\t**QTEs.** A big centred glyph and a shrinking ring. A single press within 1.2 s or a mash meter. On keyboard the key is shown. Failure costs health or an instant Policy Lapsed where the script says so, and it retries from a few seconds before. Used in: Flenser Gut, grab break, net tear, bridge run, funicular crash, cannon finale, 3 cutscene dodges. A Settings option holds single-press QTEs for mash ones.\n388\t\n389\t---\n390\t\n391\t## 10. Dialogue and writing\n392\t\n393\t**Style guide.** Write it like a B-action screenplay played completely straight, with short lines, dry comebacks and villains who love monologues. Enemies are polite: British-seaside menace (\"Mind yourself, love.\" as the gaff comes down). All voiced text shows as subtitles (§15 for the gibberish voice). Paper-based humour runs through everything.\n394\t\n395\t**Cast**\n396\t| Character | Voice |\n397\t|---|---|\n398\t| Cass Harrow | Deadpan, tired, professional. Insurance one-liners |\n399\t| Desmond Tull | Her supervisor on shortwave. Only cares about the paperwork |\n400\t| Mrs. Ottoline Vane | Acid, grand, utterly unafraid. Treats Cass as staff |\n401\t| Harbormaster Aldous Pell | Tiny, jolly, pompous, on the tannoy. Issues fines |\n402\t| Old Fathoms | The trader, bubbling and cheerful. Calls everyone \"friend\" |\n403\t| Skipper Bram | Laconic. Won't wait |\n404\t| Parishioners | Polite murmurs |\n405\t\n406\t**Canon lines, use them as written, and write the rest to match** (about 250 lines total across cutscenes, radio, barks, notes):\n407\t\n408\t- BRAM: \"Tide turns at six. I turn with it.\"\n409\t- TULL: \"Harrow, Tull. Head office wants the Vane claim closed by Friday. Total loss of one freighter, one cannery and, ah, one village.\" CASS: \"One village?\" TULL: \"It's on the form as sundries.\"\n410\t- PARISHIONER: \"Anything to declare?\" CASS: \"Only a deductible.\"\n411\t- PELL: \"Good morning, Miss Harrow! This is your Harbormaster. Section Nine of the Harbor Bylaws forbids the discharge of firearms on a public wharf. That's two shillings.\"\n412\t- PELL, later: \"Section Fourteen: loitering while alive.\" / \"Section Twenty-Two: unauthorised survival. Please remain where you are for processing.\" / \"Section Forty: damage to a parishioner. I'm afraid that's a *form*.\"\n413\t- CASS (barks): \"Put it on my tab.\" / \"Pre-existing condition.\" / \"That's coming out of your no-claims bonus.\" / \"You should've read the small print.\" / \"Act of God? I've seen God's paperwork.\"\n414\t- VANE: \"You're late.\" CASS: \"Ironbridge Mutual, ma'am. We've corresponded.\" VANE: \"You're the one who queried my dentures. Carry my bag.\"\n415\t- VANE: \"Young man, I knew your mother. She was a disappointment too.\"\n416\t- CASS: \"Get in the crate, Mrs. Vane.\" VANE: \"I will not.\" (She gets in the crate.) VANE, muffled: \"This is coming out of your premium.\"\n417\t- FATHOMS: \"Fair winds and fair prices, friend.\" / \"Bit damp, is it? Everything's a bit damp.\" / \"Mind the step. Mind the wallet.\" / \"Ooh. That's a lovely bit of scrimshaw.\" / \"Tuned her up lovely.\" / \"Come back when you're drier.\" / \"You've got a small-box look about you, friend.\"\n418\t- PELL: \"Every claim comes due, Miss Harrow. And beneath every policy, there is an Underwriter.\" CASS (looking at it): \"He's going to want to see my receipts.\"\n419\t- TULL (end): \"Harrow? Did you get a signature?\" VANE, holding out a soaked form: \"Tell your Mr. Tull his premiums are going up.\" CASS: \"Put it down as sundries.\"\n420\t\n421\t**Notes (10 short paper files, typewriter font, one screen each):** Ironbridge memo; bylaws excerpt; cannery shift notice (\"All staff to report for Communion at six. Bring own fork.\"); marine biologist's letter on *saltroot*; the skipper's tide table; Mrs. Vane's letter of complaint; Pell's fine ledger; Grice's overtime sheet; kipper recipe; Fathoms's price list (\"Everything must go. Everything does.\").\n422\t\n423\t---\n424\t\n425\t## 11. Multiplayer: Claims Rush and AI Hub\n426\t\n427\t### 11.1 Design\n428\tA 5-minute co-op wave round in a cut-down Harbor Square (`rush` level, 40×35 m). Each player is an Ironbridge temp with a seat-coloured scarf and name plate.\n429\t- All start with .38 and Sea Moss. Weapon crates (Pump, Stitcher, Rifle, Harpoon) open at 60 s intervals; first ✕ takes it.\n430\t- Waves: Parishioners from the start, Tinner at 0:45, Net-Wife at 1:30, Hounds at 2:15, Rooted at 3:00, **The Flenser at 4:00**. Enemy count scales: on screen 8 + 4 per player. Enemy HP +15% per extra player.\n431\t- **Payout (score):** kill £100, head kill +£50, follow-up +£100, chain (kills within 4 s of each other) multiplier up to ×4, revive +£300.\n432\t- **Down, not out:** at 0 HP you crawl for 20 s, and a teammate's hold ✕ revives (2 s). If everyone is down, the round ends in a loss.\n433\t- **Win:** survive to the end of the clock, or kill the Flenser.\n434\t\n435\tHub reporting is below. On its own (main menu *Claims Rush*), it plays solo or with 1 to 3 AI temps (the same bot code as §16.4), so \"Practise alone\" works and a player sees how it plays with others.\n436\t\n437\t### 11.2 Session flow (follow `tools/hub/README.md`, protocol v1)\n438\t\n439\tIn `web/index.html`, in this exact order: `<meta charset>`, the pasted `session.js` as first script, then:\n440\t```html\n441\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n442\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n443\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n444\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n445\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Survive the shift together; top payout wins\">\n446\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move, L2/RMB aim, R2/LMB fire, Cross/E kick\">\n447\t<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n448\t```\n449\tThen a small inline `window.__hub` bridge. It runs **before** the wasm block parses, so `hello` goes out at once:\n450\t- `AIHub.connect({mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true})`, queueing every event (`card`, `start`, `message`, `leave`, `time-up`, `end`) into an array Rust polls each frame as JSON.\n451\t- A `window` `keydown` listener in capture phase: before `start`, Enter → `AIHub.answer('ready')`, `M` → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Rust handles Cross and Triangle on the card and calls the same.\n452\t- On `time-up`, if host: `AIHub.finish(window.__hub.lastFinish || {standings:[AIHub.players.map(p=>p.id)]})` right there in JS. Rust publishes `lastFinish` once a second.\n453\t- `null` from `connect()` means no hub: play normally.\n454\t\n455\tRust side:\n456\t- `__hub.active` true → scene `tide/rush`, no title or menus, build the arena, call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the sim and first frame are submitted, no key press.\n457\t- Own card (egui, over the live arena): game name, players with seat colours and ready ticks, how to win, this player's controls for the device in use, time left from `card` events. No menus on it. Draw any random numbers from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n458\t- `start` → countdown → play when `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n459\t- On `end`: stop input, stop sending, silence audio.\n460\t- `AIHub.server` true → host with no local hero, slow orbit camera, no input.\n461\t- In a session: no pause (Options opens only volume settings), no quit, restart or storage writes, no `alert`, no sockets. If `navigator.gpu` is missing, call `AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU')`.\n462\t\n463\t### 11.3 Networking model (shared-world)\n464\t\n465\tOne world, run by the host. **Your own hero runs locally with no lag** and everyone trusts it. Rust RNG seed = `AIHub.seed`; never use `Math.random`.\n466\t\n467\t| Who | Sends | How |\n468\t|---|---|---|\n469\t| Client → host | Own hero: `{t:'p',x,y,z,yaw,pitch,anim}` | Unreliable, 12 Hz, `to: host` |\n470\t| Client → host | Claims: hit `{t:'h',e,part,dmg,wpn}`, pickup, revive | Reliable, batched, ≤ 5 Hz |\n471\t| Host → all | Snapshot: time, wave, enemies `[id,x·10,z·10,yaw,state,hp%]`, heroes | Unreliable, 12 Hz, ≤ 1,100 bytes (split by round-robin past 30 enemies) |\n472\t| Host → all | Events: spawn, death, attack start, fx, score, down, revive, crate | Reliable, batched, ≤ 6 Hz |\n473\t\n474\t- Stay under the limit: at most 20 messages a second per copy, 16 KB each, JSON only. Keep a token bucket in Rust.\n475\t- On every copy, mirrored characters are normal characters driven from `Game::pre` with `move_dir` toward the interpolated snapshot position (100 ms behind), so walking animation works for free. Teleport if off by more than 2 m.\n476\t- Attack and reaction events play the same clips as in the host's sim. Clients run no AI.\n477\t- A client's shots raycast against its local mirrors, show hit effects at once, then claim to the host, which applies damage and sends results. Enemy attacks land when the host says.\n478\t- Host decides standings. `finish({standings, scores:{id:payout}, won, stats:{id:{Kills,Follow-ups,Head shots,Revives}}, awards:[{id,title,detail}]})`. Awards: Top Adjuster, Kick Artist, Good Samaritan, Sharpshooter. Standings by payout, ties shared.\n479\t- On `leave`, remove the hero and let enemies retarget. `host-left` ends everything, so nothing to migrate.\n480\t\n481\t**Build order inside this feature:** first a `ghost` version (same seed, each copy its own world, others' heroes as non-colliding ghosts, `progress` + `result`), which passes the harness with 200 lines. Then upgrade to shared-world. **If shared-world still fails the harness at the end of the build, ship ghost:** change the mode meta and connect call. A passing simpler mode beats a failing better one.\n482\t\n483\t**Testing without a browser:** a cargo test that runs host + 3 clients as 4 `Sim`s in one process, passing messages through a seeded fake network with latency, jitter and loss, and bots playing all four. This finds most bugs and costs nothing. Then the harness (§17).\n484\t\n485\t---\n486\t\n487\t## 12. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller-first\n488\t\n489\t### 12.1 Rules\n490\t- Design at 1920×1080. `ctx.set_zoom_factor` so layout units are 1080p pixels at any resolution. Safe area 5%. **Minimum text 28 px, body 34 px, titles 72 px and up.** Judge from 1920×1080 screenshots.\n491\t- One column of choices, at most 7 rows. No tables, no tooltips, no dense data screens. Every screen has one job.\n492\t- Everything is reachable by pad alone, and also native on mouse and keyboard: same screens, same layout. Hover moves focus. Clicks activate.\n493\t- Fonts [V URLs], embedded with `include_bytes!`, credited in About:\n494\t  - `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/anton/Anton-Regular.ttf` for titles and numbers.\n495\t  - `.../apache/specialelite/SpecialElite-Regular.ttf` for notes and forms.\n496\t  - `.../ofl/ptsans/PT_Sans-Web-Bold.ttf` and `PT_Sans-Web-Regular.ttf` for body and subtitles.\n497\t- Palette: near-black navy plate `#0b1016` at 85%, bone text `#e9e4d8`, brass focus `#c79a3f`, teal infection accent `#4fd6c4`, red danger `#d4473a`, trader blue `#4aa8ff`.\n498\t- A focus bar slides between rows (0.08 s) with a soft tick. Confirm and back have their own sounds.\n499\t\n500\t### 12.2 Glyphs and prompts\n501\tPaint all glyphs with `egui::Painter`, no images.\n502\t- **PlayStation (default for controller):** ✕ ○ □ △ in their PS colours on dark discs, L1/R1/L2/R2 pills, sticks, D-pad with the direction lit, Options, Create.\n503\t- **Xbox (Settings option):** A B X Y in Xbox colours, LB/RB/LT/RT, View, Menu.\n504\t- **Keyboard and mouse:** keycaps with the key's name, mouse icon with the button lit.\n505\t\n506\tGame code emits action names (`Action::Reload`); only the UI turns an action plus the last device plus the glyph setting into a glyph. Test this.\n507\t\n508\t### 12.3 HUD (in play)\n509\tQuiet, big, corners only.\n510\t- **Bottom right:** ring gauge for HP (teal → amber → red), with weapon silhouette and ammo in Anton at 72 px (`10 / 34`), throwable count beside.\n511\t- **Bottom centre:** contextual prompts, glyph + verb, 40 px.\n512\t- **Top left:** Mrs. Vane's small portrait bar when with you.\n513\t- **Top centre:** boss name and bar.\n514\t- **Lower third:** subtitles on a dark plate, 40 px, speaker name in colour.\n515\t- **Objective:** a single line, appears for 5 s on change.\n516\t- Damage vignette (`hud::hit_flash` is a starting point). Cash and pick-ups flash small near the ring. No minimap in play; the Map screen has what you need.\n517\t\n518\t### 12.4 Screens (one job each)\n519\t\n520\t| Screen | Contents |\n521\t|---|---|\n522\t| Boot | DOM splash until first frame (§3) |\n523\t| Title | Live 3D harbor shot with fog and a slow camera, logo in Anton, list: Continue (if a save exists), New Claim, Chapters (after finishing the game once), Claims Rush, Settings, About. Idle 10 s → Attract. Touch-only variant below |\n524\t| New Claim | Three big difficulty cards |\n525\t| Pause | Resume, How to Play, Settings, Dev Mode, Restart Checkpoint, Quit to Title, About |\n526\t| Tackle Box | Big grid (cells ≥ 64 px) with fold-out-tray look, painted item silhouettes, one info card: name, one line, 3D turntable of the item. Pick up and place ✕, rotate R1, Use □, Combine △, close ○. Mouse: click, right-click rotates, wheel rotates, hover moves the cursor. Page: Key Items |\n527\t| Trader | Tabs Buy, Sell, Tune, with Fathoms visible in 3D at the left, a big price, cash at the top. Tune shows three fat bars. Never more than 6 rows |\n528\t| Map | Chart-style top-down drawn from the level's blocks, markers for player, objective, lamps, radios, charted treasure. Zoom L2/R2 or wheel |\n529\t| Notes | Paper on a dark table, typewriter font, ○ back |\n530\t| Log Report (save) | 4 slots as big cards |\n531\t| Chapter Report | Stats reveal one at a time with a stamped grade |\n532\t| Policy Lapsed | Reinstate, Load Log, Quit |\n533\t| Settings | Music (**default 10%**), Effects, Voice, Subtitles on/size, Glyphs (PlayStation/Xbox), Stick sensitivity, Mouse sensitivity, Invert Y, Aim assist, Rumble, Single-press QTE, Brightness, Reset. Left and right adjust, mouse drags |\n534\t| About/Credits | See §13.3 |\n535\t| Hub card | §11.2 |\n536\t\n537\t3D item views use the engine's `pav_view::assets::emit_asset` from a game overlay list (§14.1 E7): a turntable placed in front of the paused camera.\n538\t\n539\t### 12.5 Touch-only devices\n540\tTouch-only = `!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0` ([V] true on Playwright's iPhone 13 profile, false on desktop). No touch controls: turn off the engine's `touch` layer entirely. Title shows only the logo, **\"Controller or keyboard required\"**, and a Settings button. Tap works on Settings screens and that button only. Attract still starts after 10 s; a tap returns to the title. The moment a pad or key input arrives, show the normal title.\n541\t\n542\t---\n543\t\n544\t## 13. Attract, dev mode, About\n545\t\n546\t### 13.1 Attract mode\n547\tAfter **10 wall-clock seconds** with no input on the title or any main-menu screen (timed in `pav_app`, not sim ticks, so it holds at low frame rates), start the loop. Any input (key, mouse button or motion past a small threshold, pad button or stick, tap) returns to the title at once, with no save written. Music stays on the music bus.\n548\t\n549\tLoop of about 3 min: a table of beats, each `{area, start_marker, script, seconds≈18}`, driven by the bot with cheats (god, infinite ammo, teleport-if-stuck). Show as much of the demo as possible:\n550\t1. Pier arrival.\n551\t2. Square siege with shots, kicks and finishes.\n552\t3. Rooted reveal.\n553\t4. Tackle Box being used (scripted menu commands).\n554\t5. Trader Buy and Tune (scripted).\n555\t6. Gutting Floor conveyors.\n556\t7. Flenser hook and press.\n557\t8. Causeway escort and crate.\n558\t9. Bell-Hermit expose.\n559\t10. Funicular.\n560\t11. Claims Rush with AI temps.\n561\t12. Underwriter cannon shot.\n562\t\n563\tOverlay: logo, \"DEMO\" corner mark, pulsing \"Press any button\" (glyphs follow last device; \"Tap to return\" on touch-only).\n564\t\n565\t### 13.2 Dev mode (Pause → Dev Mode)\n566\tPad-driven and big, like every other screen. Tabs with L1/R1:\n567\t- **Cheats:** God, Infinite Ammo, One-Hit Kills, No Clip, Freeze AI, Slow-Mo slider, Hitboxes, Nav Grid, AI State Labels, Free Camera, Show Rank.\n568\t- **Warp:** any chapter, any checkpoint, boss rush.\n569\t- **Spawn:** any enemy at the crosshair, or a wave.\n570\t- **Give:** all weapons, ammo, £10,000, all tune-ups, all key items, heal.\n571\t- **Sliders** (live, with **Reset All** and per-row reset □). Implement as `impl Tunable for GameTuning`, so they also appear in `pav params` and `pav set path=game.x`:\n572\t  - Player: jog speed, run speed, aim-move speed, sidestep distance, yaw speed, aim assist strength, camera arm, FOV.\n573\t  - Weapons: damage ×, fire-rate ×, reload ×, headshot ×, crit chance, laser sway.\n574\t  - Enemies: HP ×, damage ×, speed ×, attack tokens, reel threshold, reel time, Rooted chance ×, spawn count ×.\n575\t  - Economy: drop rate ×, cash ×, prices ×, lamp frequency.\n576\t  - Follow-ups: kick radius, kick damage, follow-up reach.\n577\t  - Escort: Vane HP, carry speed.\n578\t  - Difficulty: Rank override.\n579\t- **Readout:** tick, fps, entity count, encounter state.\n580\t\n581\tAdd the group in `SimConfig::visit_groups` (`sim.rs`). Dev values never write to saves.\n582\t\n583\t### 13.3 About/Credits\n584\tReachable from Title and Pause. Large scrolling pages, generated at build time from the same data as the exit interview, so the two can't disagree. Pages: **Source Information** (Date, Source, Plan, Genre and Perspective, Tech, Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model, Usage = \"added on import\"), **Testing Feedback**, **Engine Feedback**, **Prompt Feedback**, **Credits** (clip libraries: CMU, Quaternius and Mesh2Motion CC0, 100STYLE CC BY 4.0 with its credit line; fonts; Pavilion engine; session client). Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm. Fill these in last, with your own real answers, not the planner's.\n585\t\n586\t---\n587\t\n588\t## 14. Art and animation\n589\t\n590\t### 14.1 Engine work needed (ordered)\n591\t\n592\t| # | Change | Where | Status |\n593\t|---|---|---|---|\n594\t| E1 | `material: Option<String>` on `Piece`, copied to `Block.material`, so legend blocks can use `material = \"MAT/cobblestone\"` | `crates/pav_core/src/level.rs` | [V] 5 lines |\n595\t| E2 | `Worn` props on bones (below) | `puppet.rs`, `pav_view/src/build.rs` | [V] 56 lines |\n596\t| E3 | Shipped pack `tide` (§14.2) | `build.rs`, `props/store.rs` | [V] 2 lines |\n597\t| E4 | `Game` hook gains `camera()`, `ui()`, `paused()`, `time_scale()`, `travel()`, `overlay()` | `games/mod.rs`, `sim.rs`, `frame.rs` | §16.2 |\n598\t| E5 | `tilt` may go negative: change `clamp(0.0, 90.0)` to `clamp(-89.0, 90.0)` in `forward()` and `up()`; apply `Game::camera` to the rig before `builder.build` | `pav_view/src/camera.rs`, `pav_app/src/app.rs`, `pav_tools/src/session.rs` (three `builder.build` calls, `capture` sees it too) | §16.2 |\n599\t| E6 | `InputFrame.look: Vec2` (radians this tick, `serde(default)`), extra button bits, `GameCmd::Tide(u16, i32, i32)`, `input look=[dx,dy]` in the tool | `input.rs`, `arpg/cmd.rs`, tools | |\n600\t| E7 | Overlay draw list from the game (laser, decals, turntable, name plates) and FX events (`SimEvent::Fx{kind,pos,dir}`, `Sfx{id,pos,gain}`, `Say{...}`) | `frame.rs`, `pav_view/src/fx.rs`, `build.rs` | |\n601\t| E8 | `NavGrid::build_floor(sim, min, max, cell, radius, floor_y, skip)`: floor top within ±0.15 of `floor_y`, obstacles between `floor_y+0.3` and `floor_y+1.6` | `nav.rs` | |\n602\t| E9 | Hand aim pose: `PuppetState.aim` (dir), `aim_w`, `aim_grip`. After `clips::over`, turn chest 40% to pitch, head along aim, put hands on the weapon with `puppet::ik` (one-hand, two-hand pistol, long gun) | `puppet.rs` `biped_skel` | |\n603\t| E10 | Device-loss guard: a `lost: Arc<AtomicBool>` set by `set_device_lost_callback`; `draw`, `resize`, `set_vsync` return early when set; sim, audio and net keep running. Once lost, try one re-create after 1 s. A boot GPU failure in a session keeps running blind | `pav_app/src/gfx.rs`, `app.rs` | Without it, a driver reset panics via a wgpu unwrap |\n604\t| E11 | Product mode: skip stats, boot panel, guide, hint bar, error panel, tuning panel, editor, studios, room card, teleports, rewind, F-keys, touch layer. Window title. Fixed render quality High | `pav_app/src/app.rs` | |\n605\t| E12 | Pointer lock and mouse delta (JS in `web/index.html`: `requestPointerLock` on click in play, `movementX/Y` accumulated, read per frame; `pointerlockchange` losing lock in play → pause). `movementX/Y` works before the lock too, so looking never depends on it. Stick to `look`. Native builds use winit | `web/index.html`, `pav_app` | |\n606\t\n607\t**E2, as verified:**\n608\t```rust\n609\t// puppet.rs\n610\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)] #[serde(default)]\n611\tpub struct Worn { pub bone: String, pub asset: String, pub pos: [f32; 3], pub rot: [f32; 3], pub scale: f32 } // Default scale 1, bone \"head\"\n612\t// add `pub worn: Vec<Worn>` to PuppetDef (default empty)\n613\tpub fn worn_frames(def: &PuppetDef, st: &PuppetState, feet: Vec3) -> Vec<(Vec3, Quat)> {\n614\t    let sk = biped_skel(def, st);\n615\t    let yaw = Quat::from_rotation_y(st.facing);\n616\t    let (q, shift) = body_motion(def, st);\n617\t    let bone_q = |a: Vec3, b: Vec3| Quat::from_rotation_arc(Vec3::NEG_Y, (b - a).normalize_or(Vec3::NEG_Y));\n618\t    def.worn.iter().map(|w| {\n619\t        let (p, r) = match w.bone.as_str() {\n620\t            \"chest\" => (sk.chest, sk.chest_rot), \"pelvis\" => (sk.pelvis, sk.pelvis_rot),\n621\t            \"upper_arm_l\" => (sk.shoulder[0], bone_q(sk.shoulder[0], sk.elbow[0])),\n622\t            \"upper_arm_r\" => (sk.shoulder[1], bone_q(sk.shoulder[1], sk.elbow[1])),\n623\t            \"lower_arm_l\" => (sk.elbow[0], bone_q(sk.elbow[0], sk.hand[0])),\n624\t            \"lower_arm_r\" => (sk.elbow[1], bone_q(sk.elbow[1], sk.hand[1])),\n625\t            \"thigh_l\" => (sk.hip[0], bone_q(sk.hip[0], sk.knee[0])), \"thigh_r\" => (sk.hip[1], bone_q(sk.hip[1], sk.knee[1])),\n626\t            \"shin_l\" => (sk.knee[0], bone_q(sk.knee[0], sk.ankle[0])), \"shin_r\" => (sk.knee[1], bone_q(sk.knee[1], sk.ankle[1])),\n627\t            _ => (sk.head, sk.head_rot),\n628\t        };\n629\t        let e = |d: f32| d.to_radians();\n630\t        let local = Quat::from_euler(glam::EulerRot::YXZ, e(w.rot[0]), e(w.rot[1]), e(w.rot[2]));\n631\t        let bone = q * yaw * r;\n632\t        (feet + q * (yaw * p) + shift + bone * Vec3::from(w.pos), bone * local)\n633\t    }).collect()\n634\t}\n635\t// pav_view/src/build.rs, emit_puppet, right after the held_asset call:\n636\tfor (w, (pos, rot)) in def.worn.iter().zip(pav_core::puppet::worn_frames(def, &p.state, feet)) {\n637\t    let at = crate::assets::Placement::at(pos).rot(rot).scale(w.scale).id(o.id.0);\n638\t    let _ = crate::assets::emit_asset(scene, &w.asset, at, 0, &Default::default());\n639\t}\n640\t```\n641\tThen in level TOML: `look = { shirt = \"#5b4632\", worn = [ { bone = \"head\", asset = \"LIB/tide/hair_hero\" }, { bone = \"chest\", asset = \"LIB/tide/jacket\" } ] }`. Add more bones if you need them. In prop coordinates, the bone's origin is the joint (head centre for head, shoulder-line centre for chest), +y up the body (down the limb is −y), +z forward. The head radius is 21 cm, so a cap's crown must be wider than 42 cm or it sinks in [V].\n642\t\n643\t### 14.2 Your asset pack [V]\n644\t- Files live in `engine/assets/props/lib/tide/<name>.json`, plus `PACK.json`.\n645\t- Add `\"lib/tide\"` to the folder list in `crates/pav_core/build.rs`, and `\"tide\"` to `SHIPPED` in `crates/pav_core/src/props/store.rs`.\n646\t- Name them `LIB/tide/<name>`. Verified working in the browser build with no `index.tsv`.\n647\t- Author with `pav asset_edit action=create` (one JSON line; `docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` is short and exact) or write the JSON directly. Check with `pav asset_preview name=x views=true figure=true`. At most two fix rounds per prop, then move on.\n648\t- Parts can use `\"mat\":\"MAT/brick_wall\"`, `\"MAT/oak_planks\"`, `\"MAT/roof_shingles\"`, `\"MAT/rough_rock\"`, `\"MAT/cobblestone\"`, `\"MAT/mossy_stone\"`, `\"MAT/wrought_iron\"`, `\"MAT/packed_earth\"`, or your own (`docs/MATERIALS.md`).\n649\t\n650\t### 14.3 Direction: engine-native toy diorama, lit like a horror film\n651\tThe engine's native look is smooth capsule puppets with dark outlines, cel shading and primitive-built props under real lights and fog. Don't fight it. Make it a **carved-and-painted fishing-village diorama, lit for horror**: chunky silhouettes, hats and coats that read at a glance, faces kept simple, and the mood coming from fog, oil lamps and the sea.\n652\t\n653\t**Baseline `[view]`, [V] tested over-the-shoulder at dawn:**\n654\t```toml\n655\t[view]\n656\t\"light.sun_elevation\" = 28.0\n657\t\"light.sun_azimuth\" = 210.0\n658\t\"light.sun_intensity\" = 0.16\n659\t\"light.ambient\" = 0.34"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"501e7141-3737-4a8e-9cac-eb3584714d8d","uuid":"0a10159f-1158-4859-b652-25e2c37b62bd","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:11:44.847Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211956__x710a06/work/PLAN.md","content":"### Chapter 3: Turning Tide (`causeway` 110×24 m and `crypt` 40×40 m, overcast dusk, rain, about 13 min)\n1. **The Causeway.** A stone spit with cover stops. The tide rises in visible steps: flooded sections slow you (×0.7) and then knock you back to the last stop if you stay. Mrs. Vane walks at 3.0 m/s and must be told Wait or Follow (§8). Parishioners rise from the water and try to **carry Mrs. Vane off** (leg shot drops her). Hounds on sandbars. Tinners in rowboats (shoot the boat's lamp).\n   - She gives Cass the **Flare Pistol** after the second attack: \"I'm not supposed to have that. Neither are you.\"\n2. **Halfway Hut.** Blue lamp and radio. Teach the crate: \"Get in the crate, Mrs. Vane.\" \"I will not.\" She does.\n3. **Chapel Yard.** Hold position while she works the sluice wheel (90 s). Co-op puzzle: two winches, one for each, cranked together to lift the crypt gate.\n4. **St. Orran's Crypt.** Boss: **The Bell-Hermit**. Mrs. Vane stays above and shouts insults.\n5. **Reward.** The Harpoon Gun on a saint's tomb. Tunnels under the rock lead to the cliffs. Chapter report.\n\n### Chapter 4: The Long Drop (`cliffs`, 100×45 m, storm, about 10 min). First to cut, see §18.\n1. **Cliff Road.** Bailiffs appear. Seal Rifle in a hunter's hut. Scuttlers. Gulls scatter.\n2. **Overwatch.** Cass on a ledge with the rifle while Mrs. Vane crosses a rope bridge (`style = \"bridge\"` chain) 60 m away, enemies at both ends. She fires flares at anything you miss. The bridge burns after she's over; Cass crosses at the run with a QTE.\n3. **The Funicular.** A 60 s scripted ride down the cliff on a moving platform. Enemies leap on, you shoot the rope brake on the other car to stop it colliding, shoot falling cargo, QTE at the end when the cable snaps (L1 + R1 together).\n4. **Lighthouse Gate.** Bailiffs drag Mrs. Vane inside as the gate drops: \"Keep your hands off the fur!\" Chapter report.\n\n### Chapter 5: The Underwriter (`lighthouse`, 30×30 m, 4 floors; then `quay` reused at storm night, flooded, about 13 min)\n1. **Lighthouse climb.** Spiral stairs and ladders, floors link by ladders enemies also use. Bailiffs, Rooted, Flenser returns on floor 3 (fight it on a narrow gallery, shoot the rail to drop it into the sea). Blue lamp on floor 2.\n2. **Lamp Room.** Pell at a desk, tiny and immaculate, the manifest in front of Mrs. Vane. He's been a puppet all along, and his jaw opens further than it should. Mrs. Vane signs with a flourish. \"That's not my signature, you little man. That's a cancellation.\" Saltroot erupts from Pell, the sea below lifts: **the Underwriter** rises in the harbor.\n3. **Boss, flooded Quay.** The same streets as Ch1, knee-deep, at night, with the storm and lighthouse beam overhead. The Square's tannoys now play only breathing.\n   - *Phase 1:* 6 glowing bulbs on tendrils around the square, each 400 HP. Tendrils sweep (dodge) and spawn Rooted.\n   - *Phase 2:* the mouth rises at the wharf. Mrs. Vane, on the radio from the lamp room, swings the beam: while it's on the mouth, the mouth flinches open for 8 s. Fetch a charge from one of 4 crate stacks, carry it (no firing) to the **Whaling Cannon** on the wharf, load (✕), aim, fire down the throat. Three charges. Waves keep coming.\n   - *Phase 3:* last charge is a QTE and the one-liner: **\"Claim denied.\"**\n4. **Escape.** A 60 s timed run from the wharf to the pier through collapsing streets; Bram's boat, Mrs. Vane already aboard, complaining.\n5. **Epilogue.** Radio. \"Harrow. Did you get a signature?\" Credits, Claim Settlement.\n\nThe last chapter in `chapters.toml` triggers ending and credits, so the ending stays valid if Ch4 is cut.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Mrs. Vane (escort)\n\n- 74 years old, 70 HP (shown top-left with her portrait). Walks at 3.0 m/s, at most 7 m behind Cass, on a flow field to Cass's feet. Never blocks a door or narrow lane: she steps aside when Cass walks into her.\n- **Follow or Wait** on D-pad down or C. On Wait she stands, or, if a **lobster crate** is within 8 m, gets in it and can't be hit. A bubble icon marks her.\n- **Enemies don't try to kill her, they carry her off:** a Parishioner with a free slot walks up, lifts her (`Walk_Carry`) and heads for the nearest exit marker. Reaching it is **game over** (\"The Harbormaster has received your client.\"). Any hit on the carrier drops her. Enemies also swing at her, 8 dmg. At 0 HP she's down for 20 s and must be helped up (✕), or the policy lapses.\n- She hits anything adjacent with her handbag: 4 dmg + short stun, every 2.5 s. From Ch3, a flare every 20 s at the nearest enemy over 6 m away, which also tells players where trouble is.\n- Your laser never harms her. Bullets stop on her with a flinch and a line (\"Do mind.\") but no damage, so she's never a tax on aim. Only explosions hurt her.\n- She reacts to low cash, big kills, and treasures with dry lines. Her lines are a big part of the game's charm: don't leave her silent.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Interactions and QTEs\n\n**World interactions** (all data-driven in level TOML, each with a prompt):\n- **Doors:** open slowly; pressing ✕ again kicks it open and knocks down anything behind.\n- **Ladders:** climb; kick a ladder down when an enemy is on it.\n- **Windows:** vault (0.8 s, invulnerable).\n- **Dressers and shelves:** push (hold).\n- **Rope:** shoot it to drop the load.\n- **Crates, barrels, lobster pots:** knife or shot breaks and drops loot.\n- **Oil barrels:** explode (3.5 m, 60 dmg, chain).\n- **Hanging lanterns:** shoot to start a 2 m fire.\n- **Valves:** steam.\n- **Winches and wheels:** hold.\n- **Fuses:** Key Item use.\n- **Radio:** save.\n- **Lamp:** trader.\n- **Notes:** read.\n\n**QTEs.** A big centred glyph and a shrinking ring. A single press within 1.2 s or a mash meter. On keyboard the key is shown. Failure costs health or an instant Policy Lapsed where the script says so, and it retries from a few seconds before. Used in: Flenser Gut, grab break, net tear, bridge run, funicular crash, cannon finale, 3 cutscene dodges. A Settings option holds single-press QTEs for mash ones.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Dialogue and writing\n\n**Style guide.** Write it like a B-action screenplay played completely straight, with short lines, dry comebacks and villains who love monologues. Enemies are polite: British-seaside menace (\"Mind yourself, love.\" as the gaff comes down). All voiced text shows as subtitles (§15 for the gibberish voice). Paper-based humour runs through everything.\n\n**Cast**\n| Character | Voice |\n|---|---|\n| Cass Harrow | Deadpan, tired, professional. Insurance one-liners |\n| Desmond Tull | Her supervisor on shortwave. Only cares about the paperwork |\n| Mrs. Ottoline Vane | Acid, grand, utterly unafraid. Treats Cass as staff |\n| Harbormaster Aldous Pell | Tiny, jolly, pompous, on the tannoy. Issues fines |\n| Old Fathoms | The trader, bubbling and cheerful. Calls everyone \"friend\" |\n| Skipper Bram | Laconic. Won't wait |\n| Parishioners | Polite murmurs |\n\n**Canon lines, use them as written, and write the rest to match** (about 250 lines total across cutscenes, radio, barks, notes):\n\n- BRAM: \"Tide turns at six. I turn with it.\"\n- TULL: \"Harrow, Tull. Head office wants the Vane claim closed by Friday. Total loss of one freighter, one cannery and, ah, one village.\" CASS: \"One village?\" TULL: \"It's on the form as sundries.\"\n- PARISHIONER: \"Anything to declare?\" CASS: \"Only a deductible.\"\n- PELL: \"Good morning, Miss Harrow! This is your Harbormaster. Section Nine of the Harbor Bylaws forbids the discharge of firearms on a public wharf. That's two shillings.\"\n- PELL, later: \"Section Fourteen: loitering while alive.\" / \"Section Twenty-Two: unauthorised survival. Please remain where you are for processing.\" / \"Section Forty: damage to a parishioner. I'm afraid that's a *form*.\"\n- CASS (barks): \"Put it on my tab.\" / \"Pre-existing condition.\" / \"That's coming out of your no-claims bonus.\" / \"You should've read the small print.\" / \"Act of God? I've seen God's paperwork.\"\n- VANE: \"You're late.\" CASS: \"Ironbridge Mutual, ma'am. We've corresponded.\" VANE: \"You're the one who queried my dentures. Carry my bag.\"\n- VANE: \"Young man, I knew your mother. She was a disappointment too.\"\n- CASS: \"Get in the crate, Mrs. Vane.\" VANE: \"I will not.\" (She gets in the crate.) VANE, muffled: \"This is coming out of your premium.\"\n- FATHOMS: \"Fair winds and fair prices, friend.\" / \"Bit damp, is it? Everything's a bit damp.\" / \"Mind the step. Mind the wallet.\" / \"Ooh. That's a lovely bit of scrimshaw.\" / \"Tuned her up lovely.\" / \"Come back when you're drier.\" / \"You've got a small-box look about you, friend.\"\n- PELL: \"Every claim comes due, Miss Harrow. And beneath every policy, there is an Underwriter.\" CASS (looking at it): \"He's going to want to see my receipts.\"\n- TULL (end): \"Harrow? Did you get a signature?\" VANE, holding out a soaked form: \"Tell your Mr. Tull his premiums are going up.\" CASS: \"Put it down as sundries.\"\n\n**Notes (10 short paper files, typewriter font, one screen each):** Ironbridge memo; bylaws excerpt; cannery shift notice (\"All staff to report for Communion at six. Bring own fork.\"); marine biologist's letter on *saltroot*; the skipper's tide table; Mrs. Vane's letter of complaint; Pell's fine ledger; Grice's overtime sheet; kipper recipe; Fathoms's price list (\"Everything must go. Everything does.\").\n\n---\n\n## 11. Multiplayer: Claims Rush and AI Hub\n\n### 11.1 Design\nA 5-minute co-op wave round in a cut-down Harbor Square (`rush` level, 40×35 m). Each player is an Ironbridge temp with a seat-coloured scarf and name plate.\n- All start with .38 and Sea Moss. Weapon crates (Pump, Stitcher, Rifle, Harpoon) open at 60 s intervals; first ✕ takes it.\n- Waves: Parishioners from the start, Tinner at 0:45, Net-Wife at 1:30, Hounds at 2:15, Rooted at 3:00, **The Flenser at 4:00**. Enemy count scales: on screen 8 + 4 per player. Enemy HP +15% per extra player.\n- **Payout (score):** kill £100, head kill +£50, follow-up +£100, chain (kills within 4 s of each other) multiplier up to ×4, revive +£300.\n- **Down, not out:** at 0 HP you crawl for 20 s, and a teammate's hold ✕ revives (2 s). If everyone is down, the round ends in a loss.\n- **Win:** survive to the end of the clock, or kill the Flenser.\n\nHub reporting is below. On its own (main menu *Claims Rush*), it plays solo or with 1 to 3 AI temps (the same bot code as §16.4), so \"Practise alone\" works and a player sees how it plays with others.\n\n### 11.2 Session flow (follow `tools/hub/README.md`, protocol v1)\n\nIn `web/index.html`, in this exact order: `<meta charset>`, the pasted `session.js` as first script, then:\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Survive the shift together; top payout wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move, L2/RMB aim, R2/LMB fire, Cross/E kick\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n```\nThen a small inline `window.__hub` bridge. It runs **before** the wasm block parses, so `hello` goes out at once:\n- `AIHub.connect({mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true})`, queueing every event (`card`, `start`, `message`, `leave`, `time-up`, `end`) into an array Rust polls each frame as JSON.\n- A `window` `keydown` listener in capture phase: before `start`, Enter → `AIHub.answer('ready')`, `M` → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Rust handles Cross and Triangle on the card and calls the same.\n- On `time-up`, if host: `AIHub.finish(window.__hub.lastFinish || {standings:[AIHub.players.map(p=>p.id)]})` right there in JS. Rust publishes `lastFinish` once a second.\n- `null` from `connect()` means no hub: play normally.\n\nRust side:\n- `__hub.active` true → scene `tide/rush`, no title or menus, build the arena, call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the sim and first frame are submitted, no key press.\n- Own card (egui, over the live arena): game name, players with seat colours and ready ticks, how to win, this player's controls for the device in use, time left from `card` events. No menus on it. Draw any random numbers from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n- `start` → countdown → play when `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n- On `end`: stop input, stop sending, silence audio.\n- `AIHub.server` true → host with no local hero, slow orbit camera, no input.\n- In a session: no pause (Options opens only volume settings), no quit, restart or storage writes, no `alert`, no sockets. If `navigator.gpu` is missing, call `AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU')`.\n\n### 11.3 Networking model (shared-world)\n\nOne world, run by the host. **Your own hero runs locally with no lag** and everyone trusts it. Rust RNG seed = `AIHub.seed`; never use `Math.random`.\n\n| Who | Sends | How |\n|---|---|---|\n| Client → host | Own hero: `{t:'p',x,y,z,yaw,pitch,anim}` | Unreliable, 12 Hz, `to: host` |\n| Client → host | Claims: hit `{t:'h',e,part,dmg,wpn}`, pickup, revive | Reliable, batched, ≤ 5 Hz |\n| Host → all | Snapshot: time, wave, enemies `[id,x·10,z·10,yaw,state,hp%]`, heroes | Unreliable, 12 Hz, ≤ 1,100 bytes (split by round-robin past 30 enemies) |\n| Host → all | Events: spawn, death, attack start, fx, score, down, revive, crate | Reliable, batched, ≤ 6 Hz |\n\n- Stay under the limit: at most 20 messages a second per copy, 16 KB each, JSON only. Keep a token bucket in Rust.\n- On every copy, mirrored characters are normal characters driven from `Game::pre` with `move_dir` toward the interpolated snapshot position (100 ms behind), so walking animation works for free. Teleport if off by more than 2 m.\n- Attack and reaction events play the same clips as in the host's sim. Clients run no AI.\n- A client's shots raycast against its local mirrors, show hit effects at once, then claim to the host, which applies damage and sends results. Enemy attacks land when the host says.\n- Host decides standings. `finish({standings, scores:{id:payout}, won, stats:{id:{Kills,Follow-ups,Head shots,Revives}}, awards:[{id,title,detail}]})`. Awards: Top Adjuster, Kick Artist, Good Samaritan, Sharpshooter. Standings by payout, ties shared.\n- On `leave`, remove the hero and let enemies retarget. `host-left` ends everything, so nothing to migrate.\n\n**Build order inside this feature:** first a `ghost` version (same seed, each copy its own world, others' heroes as non-colliding ghosts, `progress` + `result`), which passes the harness with 200 lines. Then upgrade to shared-world. **If shared-world still fails the harness at the end of the build, ship ghost:** change the mode meta and connect call. A passing simpler mode beats a failing better one.\n\n**Testing without a browser:** a cargo test that runs host + 3 clients as 4 `Sim`s in one process, passing messages through a seeded fake network with latency, jitter and loss, and bots playing all four. This finds most bugs and costs nothing. Then the harness (§17).\n\n---\n\n## 12. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller-first\n\n### 12.1 Rules\n- Design at 1920×1080. `ctx.set_zoom_factor` so layout units are 1080p pixels at any resolution. Safe area 5%. **Minimum text 28 px, body 34 px, titles 72 px and up.** Judge from 1920×1080 screenshots.\n- One column of choices, at most 7 rows. No tables, no tooltips, no dense data screens. Every screen has one job.\n- Everything is reachable by pad alone, and also native on mouse and keyboard: same screens, same layout. Hover moves focus. Clicks activate.\n- Fonts [V URLs], embedded with `include_bytes!`, credited in About:\n  - `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/anton/Anton-Regular.ttf` for titles and numbers.\n  - `.../apache/specialelite/SpecialElite-Regular.ttf` for notes and forms.\n  - `.../ofl/ptsans/PT_Sans-Web-Bold.ttf` and `PT_Sans-Web-Regular.ttf` for body and subtitles.\n- Palette: near-black navy plate `#0b1016` at 85%, bone text `#e9e4d8`, brass focus `#c79a3f`, teal infection accent `#4fd6c4`, red danger `#d4473a`, trader blue `#4aa8ff`.\n- A focus bar slides between rows (0.08 s) with a soft tick. Confirm and back have their own sounds.\n\n### 12.2 Glyphs and prompts\nPaint all glyphs with `egui::Painter`, no images.\n- **PlayStation (default for controller):** ✕ ○ □ △ in their PS colours on dark discs, L1/R1/L2/R2 pills, sticks, D-pad with the direction lit, Options, Create.\n- **Xbox (Settings option):** A B X Y in Xbox colours, LB/RB/LT/RT, View, Menu.\n- **Keyboard and mouse:** keycaps with the key's name, mouse icon with the button lit.\n\nGame code emits action names (`Action::Reload`); only the UI turns an action plus the last device plus the glyph setting into a glyph. Test this.\n\n### 12.3 HUD (in play)\nQuiet, big, corners only.\n- **Bottom right:** ring gauge for HP (teal → amber → red), with weapon silhouette and ammo in Anton at 72 px (`10 / 34`), throwable count beside.\n- **Bottom centre:** contextual prompts, glyph + verb, 40 px.\n- **Top left:** Mrs. Vane's small portrait bar when with you.\n- **Top centre:** boss name and bar.\n- **Lower third:** subtitles on a dark plate, 40 px, speaker name in colour.\n- **Objective:** a single line, appears for 5 s on change.\n- Damage vignette (`hud::hit_flash` is a starting point). Cash and pick-ups flash small near the ring. No minimap in play; the Map screen has what you need.\n\n### 12.4 Screens (one job each)\n\n| Screen | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| Boot | DOM splash until first frame (§3) |\n| Title | Live 3D harbor shot with fog and a slow camera, logo in Anton, list: Continue (if a save exists), New Claim, Chapters (after finishing the game once), Claims Rush, Settings, About. Idle 10 s → Attract. Touch-only variant below |\n| New Claim | Three big difficulty cards |\n| Pause | Resume, How to Play, Settings, Dev Mode, Restart Checkpoint, Quit to Title, About |\n| Tackle Box | Big grid (cells ≥ 64 px) with fold-out-tray look, painted item silhouettes, one info card: name, one line, 3D turntable of the item. Pick up and place ✕, rotate R1, Use □, Combine △, close ○. Mouse: click, right-click rotates, wheel rotates, hover moves the cursor. Page: Key Items |\n| Trader | Tabs Buy, Sell, Tune, with Fathoms visible in 3D at the left, a big price, cash at the top. Tune shows three fat bars. Never more than 6 rows |\n| Map | Chart-style top-down drawn from the level's blocks, markers for player, objective, lamps, radios, charted treasure. Zoom L2/R2 or wheel |\n| Notes | Paper on a dark table, typewriter font, ○ back |\n| Log Report (save) | 4 slots as big cards |\n| Chapter Report | Stats reveal one at a time with a stamped grade |\n| Policy Lapsed | Reinstate, Load Log, Quit |\n| Settings | Music (**default 10%**), Effects, Voice, Subtitles on/size, Glyphs (PlayStation/Xbox), Stick sensitivity, Mouse sensitivity, Invert Y, Aim assist, Rumble, Single-press QTE, Brightness, Reset. Left and right adjust, mouse drags |\n| About/Credits | See §13.3 |\n| Hub card | §11.2 |\n\n3D item views use the engine's `pav_view::assets::emit_asset` from a game overlay list (§14.1 E7): a turntable placed in front of the paused camera.\n\n### 12.5 Touch-only devices\nTouch-only = `!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0` ([V] true on Playwright's iPhone 13 profile, false on desktop). No touch controls: turn off the engine's `touch` layer entirely. Title shows only the logo, **\"Controller or keyboard required\"**, and a Settings button. Tap works on Settings screens and that button only. Attract still starts after 10 s; a tap returns to the title. The moment a pad or key input arrives, show the normal title.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Attract, dev mode, About\n\n### 13.1 Attract mode\nAfter **10 wall-clock seconds** with no input on the title or any main-menu screen (timed in `pav_app`, not sim ticks, so it holds at low frame rates), start the loop. Any input (key, mouse button or motion past a small threshold, pad button or stick, tap) returns to the title at once, with no save written. Music stays on the music bus.\n\nLoop of about 3 min: a table of beats, each `{area, start_marker, script, seconds≈18}`, driven by the bot with cheats (god, infinite ammo, teleport-if-stuck). Show as much of the demo as possible:\n1. Pier arrival.\n2. Square siege with shots, kicks and finishes.\n3. Rooted reveal.\n4. Tackle Box being used (scripted menu commands).\n5. Trader Buy and Tune (scripted).\n6. Gutting Floor conveyors.\n7. Flenser hook and press.\n8. Causeway escort and crate.\n9. Bell-Hermit expose.\n10. Funicular.\n11. Claims Rush with AI temps.\n12. Underwriter cannon shot.\n\nOverlay: logo, \"DEMO\" corner mark, pulsing \"Press any button\" (glyphs follow last device; \"Tap to return\" on touch-only).\n\n### 13.2 Dev mode (Pause → Dev Mode)\nPad-driven and big, like every other screen. Tabs with L1/R1:\n- **Cheats:** God, Infinite Ammo, One-Hit Kills, No Clip, Freeze AI, Slow-Mo slider, Hitboxes, Nav Grid, AI State Labels, Free Camera, Show Rank.\n- **Warp:** any chapter, any checkpoint, boss rush.\n- **Spawn:** any enemy at the crosshair, or a wave.\n- **Give:** all weapons, ammo, £10,000, all tune-ups, all key items, heal.\n- **Sliders** (live, with **Reset All** and per-row reset □). Implement as `impl Tunable for GameTuning`, so they also appear in `pav params` and `pav set path=game.x`:\n  - Player: jog speed, run speed, aim-move speed, sidestep distance, yaw speed, aim assist strength, camera arm, FOV.\n  - Weapons: damage ×, fire-rate ×, reload ×, headshot ×, crit chance, laser sway.\n  - Enemies: HP ×, damage ×, speed ×, attack tokens, reel threshold, reel time, Rooted chance ×, spawn count ×.\n  - Economy: drop rate ×, cash ×, prices ×, lamp frequency.\n  - Follow-ups: kick radius, kick damage, follow-up reach.\n  - Escort: Vane HP, carry speed.\n  - Difficulty: Rank override.\n- **Readout:** tick, fps, entity count, encounter state.\n\nAdd the group in `SimConfig::visit_groups` (`sim.rs`). Dev values never write to saves.\n\n### 13.3 About/Credits\nReachable from Title and Pause. Large scrolling pages, generated at build time from the same data as the exit interview, so the two can't disagree. Pages: **Source Information** (Date, Source, Plan, Genre and Perspective, Tech, Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model, Usage = \"added on import\"), **Testing Feedback**, **Engine Feedback**, **Prompt Feedback**, **Credits** (clip libraries: CMU, Quaternius and Mesh2Motion CC0, 100STYLE CC BY 4.0 with its credit line; fonts; Pavilion engine; session client). Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm. Fill these in last, with your own real answers, not the planner's.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Art and animation\n\n### 14.1 Engine work needed (ordered)\n\n| # | Change | Where | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| E1 | `material: Option<String>` on `Piece`, copied to `Block.material`, so legend blocks can use `material = \"MAT/cobblestone\"` | `crates/pav_core/src/level.rs` | [V] 5 lines |\n| E2 | `Worn` props on bones (below) | `puppet.rs`, `pav_view/src/build.rs` | [V] 56 lines |\n| E3 | Shipped pack `tide` (§14.2) | `build.rs`, `props/store.rs` | [V] 2 lines |\n| E4 | `Game` hook gains `camera()`, `ui()`, `paused()`, `time_scale()`, `travel()`, `overlay()` | `games/mod.rs`, `sim.rs`, `frame.rs` | §16.2 |\n| E5 | `tilt` may go negative: change `clamp(0.0, 90.0)` to `clamp(-89.0, 90.0)` in `forward()` and `up()`; apply `Game::camera` to the rig before `builder.build` | `pav_view/src/camera.rs`, `pav_app/src/app.rs`, `pav_tools/src/session.rs` (three `builder.build` calls, `capture` sees it too) | §16.2 |\n| E6 | `InputFrame.look: Vec2` (radians this tick, `serde(default)`), extra button bits, `GameCmd::Tide(u16, i32, i32)`, `input look=[dx,dy]` in the tool | `input.rs`, `arpg/cmd.rs`, tools | |\n| E7 | Overlay draw list from the game (laser, decals, turntable, name plates) and FX events (`SimEvent::Fx{kind,pos,dir}`, `Sfx{id,pos,gain}`, `Say{...}`) | `frame.rs`, `pav_view/src/fx.rs`, `build.rs` | |\n| E8 | `NavGrid::build_floor(sim, min, max, cell, radius, floor_y, skip)`: floor top within ±0.15 of `floor_y`, obstacles between `floor_y+0.3` and `floor_y+1.6` | `nav.rs` | |\n| E9 | Hand aim pose: `PuppetState.aim` (dir), `aim_w`, `aim_grip`. After `clips::over`, turn chest 40% to pitch, head along aim, put hands on the weapon with `puppet::ik` (one-hand, two-hand pistol, long gun) | `puppet.rs` `biped_skel` | |\n| E10 | Device-loss guard: a `lost: Arc<AtomicBool>` set by `set_device_lost_callback`; `draw`, `resize`, `set_vsync` return early when set; sim, audio and net keep running. Once lost, try one re-create after 1 s. A boot GPU failure in a session keeps running blind | `pav_app/src/gfx.rs`, `app.rs` | Without it, a driver reset panics via a wgpu unwrap |\n| E11 | Product mode: skip stats, boot panel, guide, hint bar, error panel, tuning panel, editor, studios, room card, teleports, rewind, F-keys, touch layer. Window title. Fixed render quality High | `pav_app/src/app.rs` | |\n| E12 | Pointer lock and mouse delta (JS in `web/index.html`: `requestPointerLock` on click in play, `movementX/Y` accumulated, read per frame; `pointerlockchange` losing lock in play → pause). `movementX/Y` works before the lock too, so looking never depends on it. Stick to `look`. Native builds use winit | `web/index.html`, `pav_app` | |\n\n**E2, as verified:**\n```rust\n// puppet.rs\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)] #[serde(default)]\npub struct Worn { pub bone: String, pub asset: String, pub pos: [f32; 3], pub rot: [f32; 3], pub scale: f32 } // Default scale 1, bone \"head\"\n// add `pub worn: Vec<Worn>` to PuppetDef (default empty)\npub fn worn_frames(def: &PuppetDef, st: &PuppetState, feet: Vec3) -> Vec<(Vec3, Quat)> {\n    let sk = biped_skel(def, st);\n    let yaw = Quat::from_rotation_y(st.facing);\n    let (q, shift) = body_motion(def, st);\n    let bone_q = |a: Vec3, b: Vec3| Quat::from_rotation_arc(Vec3::NEG_Y, (b - a).normalize_or(Vec3::NEG_Y));\n    def.worn.iter().map(|w| {\n        let (p, r) = match w.bone.as_str() {\n            \"chest\" => (sk.chest, sk.chest_rot), \"pelvis\" => (sk.pelvis, sk.pelvis_rot),\n            \"upper_arm_l\" => (sk.shoulder[0], bone_q(sk.shoulder[0], sk.elbow[0])),\n            \"upper_arm_r\" => (sk.shoulder[1], bone_q(sk.shoulder[1], sk.elbow[1])),\n            \"lower_arm_l\" => (sk.elbow[0], bone_q(sk.elbow[0], sk.hand[0])),\n            \"lower_arm_r\" => (sk.elbow[1], bone_q(sk.elbow[1], sk.hand[1])),\n            \"thigh_l\" => (sk.hip[0], bone_q(sk.hip[0], sk.knee[0])), \"thigh_r\" => (sk.hip[1], bone_q(sk.hip[1], sk.knee[1])),\n            \"shin_l\" => (sk.knee[0], bone_q(sk.knee[0], sk.ankle[0])), \"shin_r\" => (sk.knee[1], bone_q(sk.knee[1], sk.ankle[1])),\n            _ => (sk.head, sk.head_rot),\n        };\n        let e = |d: f32| d.to_radians();\n        let local = Quat::from_euler(glam::EulerRot::YXZ, e(w.rot[0]), e(w.rot[1]), e(w.rot[2]));\n        let bone = q * yaw * r;\n        (feet + q * (yaw * p) + shift + bone * Vec3::from(w.pos), bone * local)\n    }).collect()\n}\n// pav_view/src/build.rs, emit_puppet, right after the held_asset call:\nfor (w, (pos, rot)) in def.worn.iter().zip(pav_core::puppet::worn_frames(def, &p.state, feet)) {\n    let at = crate::assets::Placement::at(pos).rot(rot).scale(w.scale).id(o.id.0);\n    let _ = crate::assets::emit_asset(scene, &w.asset, at, 0, &Default::default());\n}\n```\nThen in level TOML: `look = { shirt = \"#5b4632\", worn = [ { bone = \"head\", asset = \"LIB/tide/hair_hero\" }, { bone = \"chest\", asset = \"LIB/tide/jacket\" } ] }`. Add more bones if you need them. In prop coordinates, the bone's origin is the joint (head centre for head, shoulder-line centre for chest), +y up the body (down the limb is −y), +z forward. The head radius is 21 cm, so a cap's crown must be wider than 42 cm or it sinks in [V].\n\n### 14.2 Your asset pack [V]\n- Files live in `engine/assets/props/lib/tide/<name>.json`, plus `PACK.json`.\n- Add `\"lib/tide\"` to the folder list in `crates/pav_core/build.rs`, and `\"tide\"` to `SHIPPED` in `crates/pav_core/src/props/store.rs`.\n- Name them `LIB/tide/<name>`. Verified working in the browser build with no `index.tsv`.\n- Author with `pav asset_edit action=create` (one JSON line; `docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` is short and exact) or write the JSON directly. Check with `pav asset_preview name=x views=true figure=true`. At most two fix rounds per prop, then move on.\n- Parts can use `\"mat\":\"MAT/brick_wall\"`, `\"MAT/oak_planks\"`, `\"MAT/roof_shingles\"`, `\"MAT/rough_rock\"`, `\"MAT/cobblestone\"`, `\"MAT/mossy_stone\"`, `\"MAT/wrought_iron\"`, `\"MAT/packed_earth\"`, or your own (`docs/MATERIALS.md`).\n\n### 14.3 Direction: engine-native toy diorama, lit like a horror film\nThe engine's native look is smooth capsule puppets with dark outlines, cel shading and primitive-built props under real lights and fog. Don't fight it. Make it a **carved-and-painted fishing-village diorama, lit for horror**: chunky silhouettes, hats and coats that read at a glance, faces kept simple, and the mood coming from fog, oil lamps and the sea.\n\n**Baseline `[view]`, [V] tested over-the-shoulder at dawn:**\n```toml\n[view]\n\"light.sun_elevation\" = 28.0\n\"light.sun_azimuth\" = 210.0\n\"light.sun_intensity\" = 0.16\n\"light.ambient\" = 0.34","numLines":330,"startLine":330,"totalLines":959}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013rpyb18sHXDnkqxbL3zfqk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
