{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019cPfKEY1dYebswtKnyN2nu","type":"tool_result","content":"659\t\"light.ambient\" = 0.34\n660\tsky = \"#141d28\"\n661\tfog = true\n662\tfog_start = 6.0\n663\tfog_end = 46.0\n664\thaze = 0.9\n665\thaze_height = 4.0\n666\tshafts = 0.4\n667\thalos = 1.0\n668\tbloom = 0.7\n669\tbloom_threshold = 1.0\n670\tgi = 0.8\n671\texposure = 1.15\n672\t\"cutaway.height_cut\" = false\n673\t\"cutaway.front_cut\" = false\n674\t\"cutaway.fade\" = false\n675\t```\n676\t- Variations: Ch2 sodium lamps, steam, `gi` up. Ch3 rain, `water_rain`, cold blue. Ch4 storm wind and rain, lightning (flash the `exposure` and spawn a brief light). Ch5 near-black, lighthouse beam (a moving spot built from a line of lights plus haze).\n677\t- Sea: `zone = { kind = \"water\", y0 = -2.0, y1 = -0.4, color = \"#16303a\" }` [V].\n678\t- Lights: 64 point lights, 4 of them with shadows at once (nearest). `light = {color, radius, intensity, flicker, shadows, offset}` on objects. Muzzle flash is a one-tick light.\n679\t- Blocks: floors `MAT/cobblestone`, `MAT/oak_planks`, walls via props rather than raw blocks wherever seen up close. Keep collision simple: fixed-body props with `solid` parts.\n680\t- Interiors need a ceiling (a block layer above) because the camera stays inside.\n681\t- Performance is unlimited by the brief. Add detail, props, enemies, lights and effects freely. Don't spend time optimizing.\n682\t\n683\t**Palette:** harbor greys and sea-blues, warm lamp amber `#ffb060`, blood dark red, infection bone-white with teal `#4fd6c4` glow, trader lamp electric blue `#4aa8ff`, laser red.\n684\t\n685\t**Pack contents (about 70 props; each is a short JSON):**\n686\t- **People:** hero hair, field jacket and sleeves, satchel, holster, boots. Mrs. Vane: feathered hat, fur coat body and skirt, handbag, cane. Fathoms: brass helmet with porthole, canvas body, lead boots, lantern. Pell: peaked cap, epaulettes, tiny frame via `scale`. Parishioners: sou'wester, flat cap, headscarf, oilskin torso and skirt, rubber apron, jersey collar, beards ×3, hair ×3. Flenser: iron mask, apron, winch pack, hook, chain, belly tank, belt lantern. Barnacle clusters (head, shoulder, back), Rooted chest split, bulb. Bailiff plates ×4.\n687\t- **Weapons:** service pistol (with `grip` and `tip` sockets; `weapon = { kind = \"wand\", asset = ... }` loads and draws [V], but the aim pose hid it in the test, so check its orientation early), pump, stitcher, rifle, harpoon gun and harpoon, flare pistol, knife, gaff, boat hook, oar, gutting knife, net bundle, fish-oil tin, stick, magnesium, oil lamp.\n688\t- **Quay:** cottages ×3 ([V] box walls, wedge roof, `emissive: 3` windows that glow and light the street), net loft, customs shed, harbour office, chapel front, statue of St. Orran with herring, tannoy pole, fish rack, drying nets, lobster pots, buoys, bollards, anchors, mooring chains, mail boat, foghorn tower, radio, blue lamp, tin gull, door, window, ladder, dresser.\n689\t- **Cannery:** wall sections, conveyor frame, hook rail, retort tank, valve, boiler, press with plate, fuse board, cold-store door, tin stacks, stencilled crates, catwalk.\n690\t- **Causeway and cliffs:** stone stops, sluice wheel, winch, crate, hut, funicular car and rail, rock clusters (`LIB/core/rock_cluster`), freighter hull backdrop.\n691\t- **Lighthouse:** drum wall segments, spiral stairs, gallery rail, lens, desk.\n692\t- **Creatures:** Bell-Hermit's bell shell (spawned as a prop entity moved every tick by game code), Underwriter mouth, tendrils and bulbs.\n693\t- **Generic, use `LIB/core`:** `barrel`, `crate_stack`, `basket`, `lamp_post`, `brazier`, `hand_lantern`, `candle_cluster`, `rowboat`, `fence`, `chain`, `signpost`, `well`, `table`, `chair`, `shelf`, `rubble_pile`, `rock_cluster`.\n694\t\n695\t### 14.4 Animation\n696\tNative system: procedural puppet plus clips from the library via `PuppetDef` (`idle_clip`, `walk_clip`, `run_clip`, `death_clip`) and `ch.anim.play_clip(id, flags, speed)` with `clips::UPPER | ONCE | QUICK | TRAVEL | CLAMP`. Look ids up with `clips::find`. **All of these exist [V]:**\n697\t\n698\t| Use | Clip |\n699\t|---|---|\n700\t| Hero idle, walk, jog, run | `QUATERNIUS/Idle_Loop`, `STYLE100/Neutral_Walk`, `QUATERNIUS/Jog_Fwd_Loop`, `QUATERNIUS/Sprint_Loop` |\n701\t| Aim, shoot, reload (upper body) | `QUATERNIUS/Pistol_Aim_Neutral`, `Pistol_Aim_Up`, `Pistol_Aim_Down`, `Pistol_Shoot`, `Pistol_Reload`, then E9 for long guns |\n702\t| Roundhouse, front kick, door kick | `CMU/Roundhouse_Kick`, `CMU/Front_Kick`, `MESH2MOTION/Kick_Breach` |\n703\t| Ledger Slam, finish | `QUATERNIUS/Melee_Hook`, `MESH2MOTION/Attack_Ground_Pound`, `QUATERNIUS/Sword_Regular_A` |\n704\t| Sidestep, roll, turn | `MESH2MOTION/Dodge_left`, `Dodge_right`, `Dodge_back`, `QUATERNIUS/Roll`, `MESH2MOTION/Turn_Left_180` |\n705\t| Hero hit, down | `QUATERNIUS/Hit_Chest`, `Hit_Head`, `Hit_Knockback`, `MESH2MOTION/Death_A`, `CMU/Fall_On_Face` |\n706\t| Climb, vault, push, throw | `MESH2MOTION/Climb Ladder`, `QUATERNIUS/ClimbUp_1m`, `QUATERNIUS/Push_Loop`, `QUATERNIUS/OverhandThrow` |\n707\t| Use, eat, pick up, talk | `QUATERNIUS/Interact`, `Consume`, `PickUp_Table`, `Idle_Talking_Loop`, `Idle_FoldArms_Loop`, `Yes`, `MESH2MOTION/Reject`, `Salute` |\n708\t| Parishioner walk (pick by seed) | `STYLE100/Old_Walk`, `Drunk_Walk`, `LimpLeft_Walk`, `DragLeftLeg_Walk`, `CMU/Wounded_Walk_Loop`, `STYLE100/Neutral_Walk` |\n709\t| Parishioner run, idle | `MESH2MOTION/Run_Stealth`, `MESH2MOTION/Tired Hunched`, `Idle Listening` |\n710\t| Parishioner attack | `MESH2MOTION/Sword_Attack`, `QUATERNIUS/Zombie_Scratch`, `QUATERNIUS/Melee_Hook` |\n711\t| Reel, kneel, get up, yell | `MESH2MOTION/Dizzy`, `MESH2MOTION/Kneeling Tired`, `CMU/Get_Up_Face_Down`, `QUATERNIUS/LayToIdle`, `MESH2MOTION/Zombie Yell` |\n712\t| Deaths | `MESH2MOTION/Death_A`, `Death_B`, `Death_C`, `Death_D` |\n713\t| Rooted | `MESH2MOTION/Zombie_Rise`, `Zombie_Walk`, `Zombie_Idle`, `STYLE100/Zombie_Walk` |\n714\t| Mrs. Vane | `STYLE100/Old_Walk`, `MESH2MOTION/Idle_FoldArms`, `Help_One_Arm`, `Sitting_Idle` |\n715\t| Fathoms, Flenser | `MESH2MOTION/Idle_Lantern`, `Greeting`; `MESH2MOTION/Walk_Large` |\n716\t| Carried Mrs. Vane | Carrier `MESH2MOTION/Walk_Carry`; Mrs. Vane attached by position with `Sitting_Idle` |\n717\t\n718\t**New clips** (`pav anim_edit action=create name=WORKSHOP/Name`; saved to `anim/workshop.json`, which is embedded, so `WORKSHOP/Name` works in the browser; `docs/ANIMATION_STUDIO.md`): window vault, ladder kick, net struggle, handbag swing, Pell's desk gestures, grab break, cannon load, Whaling Cannon recoil. Attack moves can also be plain data in `anim/moves.toml` (`hand = \"kick\"` etc.). Check motion with `pav filmstrip` and `animsheet`, not repeated single captures.\n719\t\n720\tWorn props follow their bones, so they move with every clip. Whips, tails and chains use the rig's verlet chains (`rig.rs`) or the soft-body rope.\n721\t\n722\t---\n723\t\n724\t## 15. Audio\n725\t\n726\tEverything is synthesized in Rust in `crates/pav_audio`, with no audio files. The mixer already runs in cpal's output in the browser [V: `Default Device @ 48000 Hz`]. `sounds_for` is a closed `match` of `Patch`es; extend, don't replace.\n727\t\n728\t**Mixer additions:**\n729\t- Buses: `music`, `sfx`, `voice`, each with its own gain. `Cmd::Bus(bus, gain)`. **Music defaults to 0.10** (Settings shows 10%), Effects 1.0, Voice 1.0.\n730\t- Per-area reverb send: a small Schroeder or FDN reverb on the mixer, set per area (cannery long and metallic, crypt huge, outdoors short).\n731\t- A sample-timed scheduler inside the mixer, so music and speech keep time at any frame rate.\n732\t- Ambient beds (waves, wind, rain, machinery hum) as looping filtered noise voices with slow LFOs.\n733\t- Biquad band-pass filters for formants and the tannoy and radio.\n734\t\n735\t**Music (all procedural patterns; state chosen by the game):**\n736\t| Cue | Sound |\n737\t|---|---|\n738\t| Title | Low drone, slow bell, a minor 6/8 shanty on a concertina-like detuned saw |\n739\t| Explore | Sparse drone, fiddle-like glides, distant foghorn |\n740\t| Combat | Boots-on-wood stomp in 7/8, low hurdy-gurdy drone, rises with enemy count |\n741\t| **Trader** | Warm major concertina waltz. The game's signature tune: make it catchy |\n742\t| Boss | Stomp + brass stabs + bell |\n743\t| Chapter report, Credits | The shanty, resolved to major at the end |\n744\t\n745\tCrossfade 1.5 s. Stinger on first Rooted, the Flenser's ratchet is an SFX and always cuts through.\n746\t\n747\t**SFX (synth patches with variation):**\n748\t- Each weapon's shot (noise burst + low thump + slide click), reload parts, dry click, shell casing.\n749\t- Footsteps by surface (cobble, plank, metal, water).\n750\t- Body hits (head distinct), kick whoosh and thud, knife, explosions (`Explosion` exists), net, whip, steam, fire.\n751\t- Crate break, door, ladder, conveyors, press, ratchet.\n752\t- Tannoy feedback squeal, foghorn (low saw + sub), bell, gulls.\n753\t- Cash, pick-up, UI tick, confirm, back, typewriter, stamp.\n754\t\n755\t**Voices (Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish).** `speak(text, voice)` schedules one blip per letter at 11 to 16 per second:\n756\t- Vowels: a saw through two band-passes at formants (a 730/1090, e 530/1840, i 270/2290, o 570/840, u 300/870).\n757\t- Consonants: 15 ms noise tick plus a short vowel.\n758\t- Pitch follows a contour: rises on `?`, falls on `.`; spaces are short rests, punctuation longer, capitals louder.\n759\t\n760\tVoices:\n761\t| Voice | Character |\n762\t|---|---|\n763\t| Cass | Mid and dry |\n764\t| Vane | Higher, 6 Hz vibrato |\n765\t| Pell | Nasal, through a 500 to 2500 Hz band-pass + crackle (tannoy) |\n766\t| Fathoms | Low, 18 Hz tremolo, 900 Hz low-pass, occasional bubble |\n767\t| Tull | Radio band-pass, hiss |\n768\t| Bram | Low and slow |\n769\t| Parishioners | Low murmur, randomized from a list, quieter |\n770\t\n771\tGibberish length follows the subtitle. Subtitle text shows as it's spoken.\n772\t\n773\t**Check by rendering, not listening (§17):** `pav audio_capture`, `render_events`, RMS per bus.\n774\t\n775\t---\n776\t\n777\t## 16. Architecture\n778\t\n779\t### 16.1 Code layout\n780\t```\n781\tengine/crates/pav_core/src/games/tide/\n782\t    mod.rs        Game impl, Phase state machine, build, travel\n783\t    hero.rs camera.rs weapons.rs combat.rs hit.rs\n784\t    ai.rs squads.rs bosses.rs escort.rs\n785\t    inventory.rs trader.rs economy.rs save.rs\n786\t    world.rs      encounters, doors, ladders, traps, pickups from level data\n787\t    script.rs     beats, cutscenes, dialogue player\n788\t    menu.rs       menu model (focus, screens, commands)\n789\t    net.rs        Claims Rush replication (pure, no IO)\n790\t    bot.rs        the bot: whole game, attract, AI temps\n791\t    tuning.rs     GameTuning: Tunable\n792\t    data/         weapons.toml enemies.toml items.toml prices.toml dialogue.toml notes.toml chapters.toml attract.toml\n793\t    levels/       quay.toml cannery.toml causeway.toml crypt.toml cliffs.toml lighthouse.toml quay_night.toml rush.toml title.toml\n794\tengine/crates/pav_ui/src/tide/      tv kit, glyphs, hud, each screen (drawn from UiFrame; also used by headless `ui`)\n795\tengine/crates/pav_view/src/tide.rs  overlay list, fx kinds\n796\tengine/crates/pav_audio/src/        buses, reverb, scheduler, music, voice, tide bank\n797\tengine/crates/pav_app/src/tide_app.rs  product mode wiring, idle timer, hub bridge, persist\n798\tengine/crates/pav_core/tests/tide.rs   the rules and playthrough tests\n799\tengine/web/index.html               session.js, metas, hub bridge, splash, pointer lock, rumble, touch-only flag, test hooks\n800\ttools/                               check, package, hub/\n801\t```\n802\t\n803\t### 16.2 The rule: all game logic lives in the sim, menus included\n804\t\n805\t**The UI is a dumb painter.** `Game` holds a `Phase` (`Title, Attract, Play, Cutscene, Menu(kind), GameOver, Report, RushCard, RushPlay, RushEnd`). Everything, including menu focus and buying a tune-up, happens in `pre`/`post` from `InputFrame`s and `GameCmd`s. So `cargo test` and the bot can walk every menu, buy items and fit them in the box without any window, which is what makes the whole game testable far faster than real time.\n806\t\n807\tHook additions (all default-implemented so `starter` keeps working; add each to `DynGame` and `GameBox` like the existing methods):\n808\t```rust\n809\tfn camera(&self, sim: &Sim) -> Option<GameCam> { None }   // target (world), yaw_deg, tilt_deg, distance, fov\n810\tfn ui(&self, sim: &Sim) -> Option<Arc<UiFrame>> { None }  // HUD and screen model; Arc so frames stay cheap\n811\tfn paused(&self) -> bool { false }                        // Sim::step runs only `pre`/`post`: no characters, no physics\n812\tfn time_scale(&self) -> f32 { 1.0 }                       // hit-stop and slow-mo, as arpg does\n813\tfn travel(&mut self) -> Option<String> { None }           // new area: rebuild like arpg::game_travel (arpg/mod.rs:404), carrying the game; bump view_serial\n814\tfn overlay(&self, sim: &Sim) -> Vec<DrawItem> { vec![] }  // laser, decals, plates, turntable: pav_view draws them\n815\t```\n816\t- **Camera** runs in the sim, so captures, tests, replays and attract all see it. App and tools set `rig.params = {yaw, tilt, distance, fov, height_offset: 0, follow_lag: 0}` and `rig.snap(target)` before each `builder.build`, interpolating between frames as they do for everything. No rig rewrite: `ground_axes`, `screen_ray` and the audio listener keep working.\n817\t- **Input:** `look` carries radians per tick. The app turns mouse delta and stick into it, `move_dir` stays world-space from `rig.relative_move`. `Sim::step` records it, so replays are exact.\n818\t- **UI commands:** `pav_ui` maps hover and click to `GameCmd::Tide(MENU_FOCUS|MENU_ACTIVATE, ...)`; pad and keys arrive as button bits. No engine `TimeControl.paused`, no `set_menu`.\n819\t- **Persist:** `UiFrame.persist: Option<String>` is written to `localStorage` by `pav_app`; at boot the app reads it and queues `GameCmd`/init so saves and settings load. Audio gains come from `UiFrame.settings` each frame.\n820\t- Follow the engine's Key rules: seeded `sim.state.rng` only, no clock, no `HashMap` iteration into state, all state in your `Clone + serde` struct (nav grids `#[serde(skip)]`).\n821\t\n822\t### 16.3 Data-driven content (the designer tools)\n823\tYour TASK.md requires infrastructure so the rest of the game could be built with normal designer tools. So all of this is data, reloaded at `load` with no rebuild via `games::level_text`:\n824\t\n825\t- **Level TOML** (`[layout]`, legend, `[[object]]`, `[[npc]]`, `[view]`, `[game]`) plus these new tables:\n826\t  - `[[encounter]] id, trigger, waves=[{enemy, count, markers, delay, max_alive}], ends_on, sets_flag`\n827\t  - `[[door]]`, `[[ladder]]`, `[[window]]`, `[[push]]`, `[[rope]]`, `[[barrel]]`, `[[valve]]`, `[[crate]]`, `[[pickup]]`, `[[tin_gull]]`, `[[note]]`, `[[lamp]]`, `[[radio]]`, `[[checkpoint]]`, `[[nav_link]] {from, to, kind}`\n828\t- **Tables:** `weapons.toml`, `enemies.toml` (stats, clip sets, wardrobe lists, drop tables), `items.toml`, `prices.toml`, `chapters.toml`, `attract.toml`.\n829\t- **Dialogue:** `[scene.<id>]` with `line = [{who, text, shot, anim, wait}]`, and a shot list per area (`eye`, `look`, `fov`, `cut|ease`).\n830\t- **Dev mode and `pav` as the editor:** `pav set path=game.enemy_hp_mult value=1.2`, `play bot=true`, `capture`, `filmstrip`, `room_check`.\n831\t- **`DESIGNERS.md`** in the dev folder, one page: how to add a level, an enemy, a weapon, a scene. Real, checked examples.\n832\t\n833\t### 16.4 The bot\n834\tOne bot serves the whole-game test, attract mode and Claims Rush AI temps. It plays through the same `InputFrame`s and `GameCmd`s a player uses.\n835\t- **Goals come from data:** each chapter lists its beats in order in `chapters.toml`, each with a bot goal: `go_to(marker)`, `interact(id)`, `clear(encounter)`, `hold(seconds)`, `buy(item)`, `tune(weapon, track)`, `fit_pickup`, `save`, `command_vane(wait|follow)`, `qte`, `boss(script)`.\n836\t- **Fighting:** pick the nearest threat, set `look` toward its head by the shortest turn, hold aim, fire within 1.5°. Press ✕ when a follow-up prompt shows, reload at empty, heal under 40% HP, sidestep when a telegraph is close, switch weapon by range.\n837\t- **Moving:** path on the nav grids with `nav_link`s for ladders and stairs. Teleport-if-stuck is allowed only with the attract cheats on.\n838\t- **Bosses:** each has a small authored script (lure, expose, shoot the weak point).\n839\t\n840\tTeach the bot each rule as you add it, as the engine's guide says. A chapter isn't finished until the bot can finish it.\n841\t\n842\t---\n843\t\n844\t## 17. Testing\n845\t\n846\t**One command:** `tools/check [sim|audio|web|hub]` (no argument = all), a Python wrapper. **It prints only failures and one final line: `checks: N passed, M failed`.** Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check (the look, composition, 10-foot legibility at 1920×1080). Keep one or two browsers open at a time. **No subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.**\n847\t\n848\t### `sim`: `cargo test -p pav_core --test tide -q` (no window, no GPU)\n849\t- **Rules:** body-part damage and reactions, follow-up availability, tokens, Rank, weapon stats from data, every tune-up, drop table.\n850\t- **Box:** fit, rotate, stack, overflow flow, combine recipes.\n851\t- **Trader:** buy, sell, tune, can't-afford, exclusive unlock.\n852\t- **Saves:** JSON round-trip restores the same status. Settings default: **music 0.10**.\n853\t- **Determinism:** same seed and inputs give same hash; record and replay.\n854\t- **Menus:** walk every screen by button bits; Back always returns; no dead focus.\n855\t- **Escort:** carried → drop on hit; reach exit → game over; crate safe.\n856\t- **Encounters:** every chapter's encounters fire and end.\n857\t- **Bot, by chapter:** the bot finishes each chapter on 3 seeds. Fair (no cheats) at Assistant for Ch1. With `god` for later chapters.\n858\t- **Whole game:** a scripted playthrough from New Claim to Credits on 3 seeds, with shopping, box use, saves and the Underwriter. The single most valuable test.\n859\t- **Careless player loses:** standing still dies.\n860\t- **Attract:** every beat runs in order and loops with no error and no save written.\n861\t- **Rush net:** host + 3 bot clients through a seeded lossy fake network: no panics, scores agree, message rate ≤ 20/s, snapshots ≤ 1,200 bytes.\n862\t- **Pack check:** every `LIB/` name in level and data files is shipped (fails on disk-only packs), all clips exist, all TOML parses with `deny_unknown_fields` on your own tables.\n863\t\n864\t### `audio`: `cargo test -p pav_audio -q`\n865\tOffline render through the mixer: each music cue non-silent at unit gain, music bus at default is 10% of unit RMS within tolerance, every SFX id non-silent and decays, voice output length follows text, voices differ. Grep the deliverable's page and `engine/` output for audio file extensions: none shipped.\n866\t\n867\t### `web`: Python Playwright against the final single HTML, from `file://`, 640×360 unless noted\n868\tExpose under `?test=1` only: `window.__gameStatus` (JSON refreshed twice a second) and `window.__gameCmds` (array Rust drains), set with `js_sys::Reflect` (adding `js-sys` needs the lock update, §3).\n869\t- Boots with no console errors or page errors; splash goes away; status phase is Title. Screenshot PNG exceeds a blank page by 1,200 bytes within 7 s at 1280×800 (hub-check's rule).\n870\t- 10 s idle → phase Attract; a key, a mouse click, a stub-pad button each return to Title.\n871\t- Stub pad (`navigator.getGamepads` returning a standard-mapping pad; see below): moves menu focus; prompts report PlayStation; Settings switches to Xbox; keyboard then reports keys; mouse hover moves focus; click activates. In play, stick changes look and position; left-click on a highlighted world object interacts.\n872\t- Pointer lock taken on click; losing it pauses.\n873\t- iPhone 13 profile: \"Controller or keyboard required\" status, Settings opens by tap, no touch controls, attract runs, then tap exits.\n874\t- WebKit and Firefox: WebGPU may be missing, in which case the page shows the \"needs WebGPU\" message with no crash.\n875\t- Audio: tap `AudioNode.prototype.connect` in an init script to an `AnalyserNode` on the destination, and check non-zero level after input.\n876\t\n877\t```js\n878\t// Stub pad, in add_init_script [V: engine sees it]\n879\tconst buttons = Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,touched:false,value:0}));\n880\tconst pad = {id:'Stub DualSense (STANDARD GAMEPAD)',index:0,connected:true,mapping:'standard',timestamp:0,axes:[0,0,0,0],buttons,vibrationActuator:null};\n881\twindow.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => { pad.timestamp = performance.now(); return [pad,null,null,null]; };\n882\t```\n883\t\n884\t### `hub`: harness with the correct flags (§3)\n885\tServe the deliverable beside `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` on `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, under a name you control. Check `window.__hubCheck.pass` after `document.body.dataset.complete`:\n886\t`players=2`, `players=3`, `players=4`, all with `&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&play=8000&auto=1`; `players=4&...&scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&...&scenario=server`. Then open the page alone: `AIHub.active` false, `Math.random` not seeded, Enter and Space pressed, no errors.\n887\t\n888\t---\n889\t\n890\t## 18. Build order\n891\t\n892\tCommit-sized stages, in this order. Each ends with its check green. Batch code edits: each pass costs a 1 to 2 minute rebuild.\n893\t\n894\t| Stage | Build | Exit |\n895\t|---|---|---|\n896\t| **0 Setup** | Clone at pin. E1, E2, E3. `tools/check` skeleton. Copy the starter to `tide`. Single-file build with `session.js`, metas, bridge, splash. Fonts | The empty game passes all hub scenarios |\n897\t| **1 Feel** | E4, E5, E6, E9, E11, E12. Hero moves, camera, aim, laser, fire at a dummy. Test room with baseline view | `capture` shows the over-the-shoulder view; pad stub and mouse drive look in browser; it feels right in filmstrips |\n898\t| **2 Fight** | Hit capsules, reactions, follow-ups, Parishioner AI, tokens, E7 FX, E8 nav, Issue .38, knife | 8 enemies vs bot in the test room; head → kick → finish chain works |\n899\t| **3 Shell** | TV kit, glyphs, HUD, Title, Pause, Settings, New Claim, Policy Lapsed, How to Play, About skeleton, touch-only, attract timer, dev mode with sliders | Menu walk tests; web suite green |\n900\t| **4 Economy** | Box, items, Trader, Tune, drops, saves, Map, Notes | Box and trader tests |\n901\t| **5 Audio** | Buses, reverb, scheduler, SFX bank, Trader waltz and Title cue, voice | Audio suite |\n902\t| **6 Ch1** | Pack first wave, full `quay`, Pell, Fathoms, Square siege, foghorn walk, Pump, report | Bot finishes Ch1, no cheats at Assistant. This is the vertical slice. Look at it at 1920×1080 and fix what's ugly |\n903\t| **7 Rush** | `rush` level, solo mode, AI temps, ghost then shared-world, own card | Rush net test; hub suite on the real game |\n904\t| **8 Ch2** | Rooted, Net-Wife, Tinner, Hounds, Stitcher, cannery machinery, fuses, Flenser, Mrs. Vane meets | Bot finishes |\n905\t| **9 Ch3** | Escort, tide, Flare, Bloats, Bell-Hermit, Harpoon | Bot finishes |\n906\t| **10 Ch5** | Lighthouse, Bailiffs, `quay_night`, Underwriter, cannon, escape, ending, credits | **Whole-game test passes** (Ch4 absent) |\n907\t| **11 Ch4** | Rifle, Overwatch, bridge, funicular | Whole-game test still passes |\n908\t| **12 Finish** | Attract loop complete, all music and barks, notes, Tin Gulls, Exclusives, Actuary, DESIGNERS.md, About pages from real answers, exit interview, final packaging | `tools/check` all green; §19 walked line by line |\n909\t\n910\t**If you run short, cut in this order and nothing else:**\n911\t1. Tin Gulls and Exclusives.\n912\t2. Ch4's Overwatch.\n913\t3. Ch4 entirely (add the Seal Rifle to the Ch3 trader, and go by tunnel to the lighthouse with Mrs. Vane captured there).\n914\t4. Actuary and costumes.\n915\t\n916\t**Never cut:** attract, dev mode, hub passing, settings, glyphs, touch-only screen, About, the Flenser, the Bell-Hermit, the Underwriter, the foghorn walk.\n917\t\n918\tYour brief's \"Done\" rule stands: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. If something's cut, it's gone from menus, code paths and text, not greyed out.\n919\t\n920\t---\n921\t\n922\t## 19. Delivery and full brief coverage\n923\t\n924\t**Package:** `tools/package` runs `build-web.sh --single-file --scene tide --title \"<title>\" ...` with `--out` pointing at the deliverable path your TASK.md names. Then run `tools/check`. When done, delete `engine/target` and any `node_modules` (2 GB+, rebuildable). Keep source. Keep all files inside your dev folder and the folder root your TASK.md gives, not `/tmp`. Stop only processes you started, by PID.\n925\t\n926\t**Engine feedback notes:** keep a short running list as you go, since your TASK.md asks what you changed and where you got stuck. §14.1 is most of it.\n927\t\n928\t**Final reply:** put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply as well as on the About screen. Further research is your choice. Report what you actually did, adding that this plan's research covered the engine source and the hub protocol.\n929\t\n930\t**Exit interview:** fill in the exit-interview file your TASK.md describes, with your own answers, and check it parses as JSON. Catalogue values for this game: type Game; genre Horror; source Resident Evil 4; series Resident Evil; players 1–4; tags such as `3d`, `third-person`, `co-op`, `horror`, `story`, `boss fights`.\n931\t\n932\t| Brief asks for | Where |\n933\t|---|---|\n934\t| Original game inspired by the source; world, characters, themes, tone turned into mechanics | §1, §2, §5 to §10 |\n935\t| Genre and perspective chosen | §1 |\n936\t| Title: riff, picked with a real RNG from 50 | Yours; intro of this plan |\n937\t| Single HTML package | §3, §19 |\n938\t| Dev subfolder; don't read outside; port and process rules | §3, §17, §19 |\n939\t| Build on the shardfall engine, change anything | §3, §14.1, §16 |\n940\t| Native art style as base, new art for the source's feel, library for generics | §14 |\n941\t| Native animation as base, new animations | §14.4 |\n942\t| All audio in code, gibberish voices, music 10% default | §15, §12.4, §17 |\n943\t| Online: hub integration and game on its own | §11, §17 |\n944\t| Performance budget unlimited, no optimization | §14.3 |\n945\t| Headless tests, one command, failures and one-line count, whole-game playthrough, few screenshots, no review subagents | §17 |\n946\t| Feature-complete vertical slice, long enough to show everything, what you can and can't do | §1, §4.3, §7 |\n947\t| Infrastructure for later content with designer tools | §16.3 |\n948\t| Dev mode from pause, standard tools, live sliders, reset | §13.2 |\n949\t| Attract: 10 s idle, looping, AI-played, cheats allowed, any input exits | §13.1 |\n950\t| Multiplayer | §11 |\n951\t| Narrative style like the source's | §10 |\n952\t| Controller-first 10-foot; DualSense standard mapping; native KB and mouse; mouse clicks menu items and world things; hover moves focus | §4.1, §12, §9 |\n953\t| Prompts follow last input; PS glyphs, Xbox option in Settings; keys and mouse | §12.2 |\n954\t| No dense web-style screens | §12.1 |\n955\t| Touch-only: message, settings button, attract runs, no touch controls | §12.5 |\n956\t| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §18 |\n957\t| Source Information, Testing, Engine, Prompt Feedback, in chat reply and in-game About | §13.3 |\n958\t| Exit interview file | §19 |\n959\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"501e7141-3737-4a8e-9cac-eb3584714d8d","uuid":"ca72cee9-4960-421b-8355-d182e8491903","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:12:00.645Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211956__x710a06/work/PLAN.md","content":"\"light.ambient\" = 0.34\nsky = \"#141d28\"\nfog = true\nfog_start = 6.0\nfog_end = 46.0\nhaze = 0.9\nhaze_height = 4.0\nshafts = 0.4\nhalos = 1.0\nbloom = 0.7\nbloom_threshold = 1.0\ngi = 0.8\nexposure = 1.15\n\"cutaway.height_cut\" = false\n\"cutaway.front_cut\" = false\n\"cutaway.fade\" = false\n```\n- Variations: Ch2 sodium lamps, steam, `gi` up. Ch3 rain, `water_rain`, cold blue. Ch4 storm wind and rain, lightning (flash the `exposure` and spawn a brief light). Ch5 near-black, lighthouse beam (a moving spot built from a line of lights plus haze).\n- Sea: `zone = { kind = \"water\", y0 = -2.0, y1 = -0.4, color = \"#16303a\" }` [V].\n- Lights: 64 point lights, 4 of them with shadows at once (nearest). `light = {color, radius, intensity, flicker, shadows, offset}` on objects. Muzzle flash is a one-tick light.\n- Blocks: floors `MAT/cobblestone`, `MAT/oak_planks`, walls via props rather than raw blocks wherever seen up close. Keep collision simple: fixed-body props with `solid` parts.\n- Interiors need a ceiling (a block layer above) because the camera stays inside.\n- Performance is unlimited by the brief. Add detail, props, enemies, lights and effects freely. Don't spend time optimizing.\n\n**Palette:** harbor greys and sea-blues, warm lamp amber `#ffb060`, blood dark red, infection bone-white with teal `#4fd6c4` glow, trader lamp electric blue `#4aa8ff`, laser red.\n\n**Pack contents (about 70 props; each is a short JSON):**\n- **People:** hero hair, field jacket and sleeves, satchel, holster, boots. Mrs. Vane: feathered hat, fur coat body and skirt, handbag, cane. Fathoms: brass helmet with porthole, canvas body, lead boots, lantern. Pell: peaked cap, epaulettes, tiny frame via `scale`. Parishioners: sou'wester, flat cap, headscarf, oilskin torso and skirt, rubber apron, jersey collar, beards ×3, hair ×3. Flenser: iron mask, apron, winch pack, hook, chain, belly tank, belt lantern. Barnacle clusters (head, shoulder, back), Rooted chest split, bulb. Bailiff plates ×4.\n- **Weapons:** service pistol (with `grip` and `tip` sockets; `weapon = { kind = \"wand\", asset = ... }` loads and draws [V], but the aim pose hid it in the test, so check its orientation early), pump, stitcher, rifle, harpoon gun and harpoon, flare pistol, knife, gaff, boat hook, oar, gutting knife, net bundle, fish-oil tin, stick, magnesium, oil lamp.\n- **Quay:** cottages ×3 ([V] box walls, wedge roof, `emissive: 3` windows that glow and light the street), net loft, customs shed, harbour office, chapel front, statue of St. Orran with herring, tannoy pole, fish rack, drying nets, lobster pots, buoys, bollards, anchors, mooring chains, mail boat, foghorn tower, radio, blue lamp, tin gull, door, window, ladder, dresser.\n- **Cannery:** wall sections, conveyor frame, hook rail, retort tank, valve, boiler, press with plate, fuse board, cold-store door, tin stacks, stencilled crates, catwalk.\n- **Causeway and cliffs:** stone stops, sluice wheel, winch, crate, hut, funicular car and rail, rock clusters (`LIB/core/rock_cluster`), freighter hull backdrop.\n- **Lighthouse:** drum wall segments, spiral stairs, gallery rail, lens, desk.\n- **Creatures:** Bell-Hermit's bell shell (spawned as a prop entity moved every tick by game code), Underwriter mouth, tendrils and bulbs.\n- **Generic, use `LIB/core`:** `barrel`, `crate_stack`, `basket`, `lamp_post`, `brazier`, `hand_lantern`, `candle_cluster`, `rowboat`, `fence`, `chain`, `signpost`, `well`, `table`, `chair`, `shelf`, `rubble_pile`, `rock_cluster`.\n\n### 14.4 Animation\nNative system: procedural puppet plus clips from the library via `PuppetDef` (`idle_clip`, `walk_clip`, `run_clip`, `death_clip`) and `ch.anim.play_clip(id, flags, speed)` with `clips::UPPER | ONCE | QUICK | TRAVEL | CLAMP`. Look ids up with `clips::find`. **All of these exist [V]:**\n\n| Use | Clip |\n|---|---|\n| Hero idle, walk, jog, run | `QUATERNIUS/Idle_Loop`, `STYLE100/Neutral_Walk`, `QUATERNIUS/Jog_Fwd_Loop`, `QUATERNIUS/Sprint_Loop` |\n| Aim, shoot, reload (upper body) | `QUATERNIUS/Pistol_Aim_Neutral`, `Pistol_Aim_Up`, `Pistol_Aim_Down`, `Pistol_Shoot`, `Pistol_Reload`, then E9 for long guns |\n| Roundhouse, front kick, door kick | `CMU/Roundhouse_Kick`, `CMU/Front_Kick`, `MESH2MOTION/Kick_Breach` |\n| Ledger Slam, finish | `QUATERNIUS/Melee_Hook`, `MESH2MOTION/Attack_Ground_Pound`, `QUATERNIUS/Sword_Regular_A` |\n| Sidestep, roll, turn | `MESH2MOTION/Dodge_left`, `Dodge_right`, `Dodge_back`, `QUATERNIUS/Roll`, `MESH2MOTION/Turn_Left_180` |\n| Hero hit, down | `QUATERNIUS/Hit_Chest`, `Hit_Head`, `Hit_Knockback`, `MESH2MOTION/Death_A`, `CMU/Fall_On_Face` |\n| Climb, vault, push, throw | `MESH2MOTION/Climb Ladder`, `QUATERNIUS/ClimbUp_1m`, `QUATERNIUS/Push_Loop`, `QUATERNIUS/OverhandThrow` |\n| Use, eat, pick up, talk | `QUATERNIUS/Interact`, `Consume`, `PickUp_Table`, `Idle_Talking_Loop`, `Idle_FoldArms_Loop`, `Yes`, `MESH2MOTION/Reject`, `Salute` |\n| Parishioner walk (pick by seed) | `STYLE100/Old_Walk`, `Drunk_Walk`, `LimpLeft_Walk`, `DragLeftLeg_Walk`, `CMU/Wounded_Walk_Loop`, `STYLE100/Neutral_Walk` |\n| Parishioner run, idle | `MESH2MOTION/Run_Stealth`, `MESH2MOTION/Tired Hunched`, `Idle Listening` |\n| Parishioner attack | `MESH2MOTION/Sword_Attack`, `QUATERNIUS/Zombie_Scratch`, `QUATERNIUS/Melee_Hook` |\n| Reel, kneel, get up, yell | `MESH2MOTION/Dizzy`, `MESH2MOTION/Kneeling Tired`, `CMU/Get_Up_Face_Down`, `QUATERNIUS/LayToIdle`, `MESH2MOTION/Zombie Yell` |\n| Deaths | `MESH2MOTION/Death_A`, `Death_B`, `Death_C`, `Death_D` |\n| Rooted | `MESH2MOTION/Zombie_Rise`, `Zombie_Walk`, `Zombie_Idle`, `STYLE100/Zombie_Walk` |\n| Mrs. Vane | `STYLE100/Old_Walk`, `MESH2MOTION/Idle_FoldArms`, `Help_One_Arm`, `Sitting_Idle` |\n| Fathoms, Flenser | `MESH2MOTION/Idle_Lantern`, `Greeting`; `MESH2MOTION/Walk_Large` |\n| Carried Mrs. Vane | Carrier `MESH2MOTION/Walk_Carry`; Mrs. Vane attached by position with `Sitting_Idle` |\n\n**New clips** (`pav anim_edit action=create name=WORKSHOP/Name`; saved to `anim/workshop.json`, which is embedded, so `WORKSHOP/Name` works in the browser; `docs/ANIMATION_STUDIO.md`): window vault, ladder kick, net struggle, handbag swing, Pell's desk gestures, grab break, cannon load, Whaling Cannon recoil. Attack moves can also be plain data in `anim/moves.toml` (`hand = \"kick\"` etc.). Check motion with `pav filmstrip` and `animsheet`, not repeated single captures.\n\nWorn props follow their bones, so they move with every clip. Whips, tails and chains use the rig's verlet chains (`rig.rs`) or the soft-body rope.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Audio\n\nEverything is synthesized in Rust in `crates/pav_audio`, with no audio files. The mixer already runs in cpal's output in the browser [V: `Default Device @ 48000 Hz`]. `sounds_for` is a closed `match` of `Patch`es; extend, don't replace.\n\n**Mixer additions:**\n- Buses: `music`, `sfx`, `voice`, each with its own gain. `Cmd::Bus(bus, gain)`. **Music defaults to 0.10** (Settings shows 10%), Effects 1.0, Voice 1.0.\n- Per-area reverb send: a small Schroeder or FDN reverb on the mixer, set per area (cannery long and metallic, crypt huge, outdoors short).\n- A sample-timed scheduler inside the mixer, so music and speech keep time at any frame rate.\n- Ambient beds (waves, wind, rain, machinery hum) as looping filtered noise voices with slow LFOs.\n- Biquad band-pass filters for formants and the tannoy and radio.\n\n**Music (all procedural patterns; state chosen by the game):**\n| Cue | Sound |\n|---|---|\n| Title | Low drone, slow bell, a minor 6/8 shanty on a concertina-like detuned saw |\n| Explore | Sparse drone, fiddle-like glides, distant foghorn |\n| Combat | Boots-on-wood stomp in 7/8, low hurdy-gurdy drone, rises with enemy count |\n| **Trader** | Warm major concertina waltz. The game's signature tune: make it catchy |\n| Boss | Stomp + brass stabs + bell |\n| Chapter report, Credits | The shanty, resolved to major at the end |\n\nCrossfade 1.5 s. Stinger on first Rooted, the Flenser's ratchet is an SFX and always cuts through.\n\n**SFX (synth patches with variation):**\n- Each weapon's shot (noise burst + low thump + slide click), reload parts, dry click, shell casing.\n- Footsteps by surface (cobble, plank, metal, water).\n- Body hits (head distinct), kick whoosh and thud, knife, explosions (`Explosion` exists), net, whip, steam, fire.\n- Crate break, door, ladder, conveyors, press, ratchet.\n- Tannoy feedback squeal, foghorn (low saw + sub), bell, gulls.\n- Cash, pick-up, UI tick, confirm, back, typewriter, stamp.\n\n**Voices (Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish).** `speak(text, voice)` schedules one blip per letter at 11 to 16 per second:\n- Vowels: a saw through two band-passes at formants (a 730/1090, e 530/1840, i 270/2290, o 570/840, u 300/870).\n- Consonants: 15 ms noise tick plus a short vowel.\n- Pitch follows a contour: rises on `?`, falls on `.`; spaces are short rests, punctuation longer, capitals louder.\n\nVoices:\n| Voice | Character |\n|---|---|\n| Cass | Mid and dry |\n| Vane | Higher, 6 Hz vibrato |\n| Pell | Nasal, through a 500 to 2500 Hz band-pass + crackle (tannoy) |\n| Fathoms | Low, 18 Hz tremolo, 900 Hz low-pass, occasional bubble |\n| Tull | Radio band-pass, hiss |\n| Bram | Low and slow |\n| Parishioners | Low murmur, randomized from a list, quieter |\n\nGibberish length follows the subtitle. Subtitle text shows as it's spoken.\n\n**Check by rendering, not listening (§17):** `pav audio_capture`, `render_events`, RMS per bus.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Architecture\n\n### 16.1 Code layout\n```\nengine/crates/pav_core/src/games/tide/\n    mod.rs        Game impl, Phase state machine, build, travel\n    hero.rs camera.rs weapons.rs combat.rs hit.rs\n    ai.rs squads.rs bosses.rs escort.rs\n    inventory.rs trader.rs economy.rs save.rs\n    world.rs      encounters, doors, ladders, traps, pickups from level data\n    script.rs     beats, cutscenes, dialogue player\n    menu.rs       menu model (focus, screens, commands)\n    net.rs        Claims Rush replication (pure, no IO)\n    bot.rs        the bot: whole game, attract, AI temps\n    tuning.rs     GameTuning: Tunable\n    data/         weapons.toml enemies.toml items.toml prices.toml dialogue.toml notes.toml chapters.toml attract.toml\n    levels/       quay.toml cannery.toml causeway.toml crypt.toml cliffs.toml lighthouse.toml quay_night.toml rush.toml title.toml\nengine/crates/pav_ui/src/tide/      tv kit, glyphs, hud, each screen (drawn from UiFrame; also used by headless `ui`)\nengine/crates/pav_view/src/tide.rs  overlay list, fx kinds\nengine/crates/pav_audio/src/        buses, reverb, scheduler, music, voice, tide bank\nengine/crates/pav_app/src/tide_app.rs  product mode wiring, idle timer, hub bridge, persist\nengine/crates/pav_core/tests/tide.rs   the rules and playthrough tests\nengine/web/index.html               session.js, metas, hub bridge, splash, pointer lock, rumble, touch-only flag, test hooks\ntools/                               check, package, hub/\n```\n\n### 16.2 The rule: all game logic lives in the sim, menus included\n\n**The UI is a dumb painter.** `Game` holds a `Phase` (`Title, Attract, Play, Cutscene, Menu(kind), GameOver, Report, RushCard, RushPlay, RushEnd`). Everything, including menu focus and buying a tune-up, happens in `pre`/`post` from `InputFrame`s and `GameCmd`s. So `cargo test` and the bot can walk every menu, buy items and fit them in the box without any window, which is what makes the whole game testable far faster than real time.\n\nHook additions (all default-implemented so `starter` keeps working; add each to `DynGame` and `GameBox` like the existing methods):\n```rust\nfn camera(&self, sim: &Sim) -> Option<GameCam> { None }   // target (world), yaw_deg, tilt_deg, distance, fov\nfn ui(&self, sim: &Sim) -> Option<Arc<UiFrame>> { None }  // HUD and screen model; Arc so frames stay cheap\nfn paused(&self) -> bool { false }                        // Sim::step runs only `pre`/`post`: no characters, no physics\nfn time_scale(&self) -> f32 { 1.0 }                       // hit-stop and slow-mo, as arpg does\nfn travel(&mut self) -> Option<String> { None }           // new area: rebuild like arpg::game_travel (arpg/mod.rs:404), carrying the game; bump view_serial\nfn overlay(&self, sim: &Sim) -> Vec<DrawItem> { vec![] }  // laser, decals, plates, turntable: pav_view draws them\n```\n- **Camera** runs in the sim, so captures, tests, replays and attract all see it. App and tools set `rig.params = {yaw, tilt, distance, fov, height_offset: 0, follow_lag: 0}` and `rig.snap(target)` before each `builder.build`, interpolating between frames as they do for everything. No rig rewrite: `ground_axes`, `screen_ray` and the audio listener keep working.\n- **Input:** `look` carries radians per tick. The app turns mouse delta and stick into it, `move_dir` stays world-space from `rig.relative_move`. `Sim::step` records it, so replays are exact.\n- **UI commands:** `pav_ui` maps hover and click to `GameCmd::Tide(MENU_FOCUS|MENU_ACTIVATE, ...)`; pad and keys arrive as button bits. No engine `TimeControl.paused`, no `set_menu`.\n- **Persist:** `UiFrame.persist: Option<String>` is written to `localStorage` by `pav_app`; at boot the app reads it and queues `GameCmd`/init so saves and settings load. Audio gains come from `UiFrame.settings` each frame.\n- Follow the engine's Key rules: seeded `sim.state.rng` only, no clock, no `HashMap` iteration into state, all state in your `Clone + serde` struct (nav grids `#[serde(skip)]`).\n\n### 16.3 Data-driven content (the designer tools)\nYour TASK.md requires infrastructure so the rest of the game could be built with normal designer tools. So all of this is data, reloaded at `load` with no rebuild via `games::level_text`:\n\n- **Level TOML** (`[layout]`, legend, `[[object]]`, `[[npc]]`, `[view]`, `[game]`) plus these new tables:\n  - `[[encounter]] id, trigger, waves=[{enemy, count, markers, delay, max_alive}], ends_on, sets_flag`\n  - `[[door]]`, `[[ladder]]`, `[[window]]`, `[[push]]`, `[[rope]]`, `[[barrel]]`, `[[valve]]`, `[[crate]]`, `[[pickup]]`, `[[tin_gull]]`, `[[note]]`, `[[lamp]]`, `[[radio]]`, `[[checkpoint]]`, `[[nav_link]] {from, to, kind}`\n- **Tables:** `weapons.toml`, `enemies.toml` (stats, clip sets, wardrobe lists, drop tables), `items.toml`, `prices.toml`, `chapters.toml`, `attract.toml`.\n- **Dialogue:** `[scene.<id>]` with `line = [{who, text, shot, anim, wait}]`, and a shot list per area (`eye`, `look`, `fov`, `cut|ease`).\n- **Dev mode and `pav` as the editor:** `pav set path=game.enemy_hp_mult value=1.2`, `play bot=true`, `capture`, `filmstrip`, `room_check`.\n- **`DESIGNERS.md`** in the dev folder, one page: how to add a level, an enemy, a weapon, a scene. Real, checked examples.\n\n### 16.4 The bot\nOne bot serves the whole-game test, attract mode and Claims Rush AI temps. It plays through the same `InputFrame`s and `GameCmd`s a player uses.\n- **Goals come from data:** each chapter lists its beats in order in `chapters.toml`, each with a bot goal: `go_to(marker)`, `interact(id)`, `clear(encounter)`, `hold(seconds)`, `buy(item)`, `tune(weapon, track)`, `fit_pickup`, `save`, `command_vane(wait|follow)`, `qte`, `boss(script)`.\n- **Fighting:** pick the nearest threat, set `look` toward its head by the shortest turn, hold aim, fire within 1.5°. Press ✕ when a follow-up prompt shows, reload at empty, heal under 40% HP, sidestep when a telegraph is close, switch weapon by range.\n- **Moving:** path on the nav grids with `nav_link`s for ladders and stairs. Teleport-if-stuck is allowed only with the attract cheats on.\n- **Bosses:** each has a small authored script (lure, expose, shoot the weak point).\n\nTeach the bot each rule as you add it, as the engine's guide says. A chapter isn't finished until the bot can finish it.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Testing\n\n**One command:** `tools/check [sim|audio|web|hub]` (no argument = all), a Python wrapper. **It prints only failures and one final line: `checks: N passed, M failed`.** Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check (the look, composition, 10-foot legibility at 1920×1080). Keep one or two browsers open at a time. **No subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.**\n\n### `sim`: `cargo test -p pav_core --test tide -q` (no window, no GPU)\n- **Rules:** body-part damage and reactions, follow-up availability, tokens, Rank, weapon stats from data, every tune-up, drop table.\n- **Box:** fit, rotate, stack, overflow flow, combine recipes.\n- **Trader:** buy, sell, tune, can't-afford, exclusive unlock.\n- **Saves:** JSON round-trip restores the same status. Settings default: **music 0.10**.\n- **Determinism:** same seed and inputs give same hash; record and replay.\n- **Menus:** walk every screen by button bits; Back always returns; no dead focus.\n- **Escort:** carried → drop on hit; reach exit → game over; crate safe.\n- **Encounters:** every chapter's encounters fire and end.\n- **Bot, by chapter:** the bot finishes each chapter on 3 seeds. Fair (no cheats) at Assistant for Ch1. With `god` for later chapters.\n- **Whole game:** a scripted playthrough from New Claim to Credits on 3 seeds, with shopping, box use, saves and the Underwriter. The single most valuable test.\n- **Careless player loses:** standing still dies.\n- **Attract:** every beat runs in order and loops with no error and no save written.\n- **Rush net:** host + 3 bot clients through a seeded lossy fake network: no panics, scores agree, message rate ≤ 20/s, snapshots ≤ 1,200 bytes.\n- **Pack check:** every `LIB/` name in level and data files is shipped (fails on disk-only packs), all clips exist, all TOML parses with `deny_unknown_fields` on your own tables.\n\n### `audio`: `cargo test -p pav_audio -q`\nOffline render through the mixer: each music cue non-silent at unit gain, music bus at default is 10% of unit RMS within tolerance, every SFX id non-silent and decays, voice output length follows text, voices differ. Grep the deliverable's page and `engine/` output for audio file extensions: none shipped.\n\n### `web`: Python Playwright against the final single HTML, from `file://`, 640×360 unless noted\nExpose under `?test=1` only: `window.__gameStatus` (JSON refreshed twice a second) and `window.__gameCmds` (array Rust drains), set with `js_sys::Reflect` (adding `js-sys` needs the lock update, §3).\n- Boots with no console errors or page errors; splash goes away; status phase is Title. Screenshot PNG exceeds a blank page by 1,200 bytes within 7 s at 1280×800 (hub-check's rule).\n- 10 s idle → phase Attract; a key, a mouse click, a stub-pad button each return to Title.\n- Stub pad (`navigator.getGamepads` returning a standard-mapping pad; see below): moves menu focus; prompts report PlayStation; Settings switches to Xbox; keyboard then reports keys; mouse hover moves focus; click activates. In play, stick changes look and position; left-click on a highlighted world object interacts.\n- Pointer lock taken on click; losing it pauses.\n- iPhone 13 profile: \"Controller or keyboard required\" status, Settings opens by tap, no touch controls, attract runs, then tap exits.\n- WebKit and Firefox: WebGPU may be missing, in which case the page shows the \"needs WebGPU\" message with no crash.\n- Audio: tap `AudioNode.prototype.connect` in an init script to an `AnalyserNode` on the destination, and check non-zero level after input.\n\n```js\n// Stub pad, in add_init_script [V: engine sees it]\nconst buttons = Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,touched:false,value:0}));\nconst pad = {id:'Stub DualSense (STANDARD GAMEPAD)',index:0,connected:true,mapping:'standard',timestamp:0,axes:[0,0,0,0],buttons,vibrationActuator:null};\nwindow.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => { pad.timestamp = performance.now(); return [pad,null,null,null]; };\n```\n\n### `hub`: harness with the correct flags (§3)\nServe the deliverable beside `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` on `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, under a name you control. Check `window.__hubCheck.pass` after `document.body.dataset.complete`:\n`players=2`, `players=3`, `players=4`, all with `&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&play=8000&auto=1`; `players=4&...&scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&...&scenario=server`. Then open the page alone: `AIHub.active` false, `Math.random` not seeded, Enter and Space pressed, no errors.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Build order\n\nCommit-sized stages, in this order. Each ends with its check green. Batch code edits: each pass costs a 1 to 2 minute rebuild.\n\n| Stage | Build | Exit |\n|---|---|---|\n| **0 Setup** | Clone at pin. E1, E2, E3. `tools/check` skeleton. Copy the starter to `tide`. Single-file build with `session.js`, metas, bridge, splash. Fonts | The empty game passes all hub scenarios |\n| **1 Feel** | E4, E5, E6, E9, E11, E12. Hero moves, camera, aim, laser, fire at a dummy. Test room with baseline view | `capture` shows the over-the-shoulder view; pad stub and mouse drive look in browser; it feels right in filmstrips |\n| **2 Fight** | Hit capsules, reactions, follow-ups, Parishioner AI, tokens, E7 FX, E8 nav, Issue .38, knife | 8 enemies vs bot in the test room; head → kick → finish chain works |\n| **3 Shell** | TV kit, glyphs, HUD, Title, Pause, Settings, New Claim, Policy Lapsed, How to Play, About skeleton, touch-only, attract timer, dev mode with sliders | Menu walk tests; web suite green |\n| **4 Economy** | Box, items, Trader, Tune, drops, saves, Map, Notes | Box and trader tests |\n| **5 Audio** | Buses, reverb, scheduler, SFX bank, Trader waltz and Title cue, voice | Audio suite |\n| **6 Ch1** | Pack first wave, full `quay`, Pell, Fathoms, Square siege, foghorn walk, Pump, report | Bot finishes Ch1, no cheats at Assistant. This is the vertical slice. Look at it at 1920×1080 and fix what's ugly |\n| **7 Rush** | `rush` level, solo mode, AI temps, ghost then shared-world, own card | Rush net test; hub suite on the real game |\n| **8 Ch2** | Rooted, Net-Wife, Tinner, Hounds, Stitcher, cannery machinery, fuses, Flenser, Mrs. Vane meets | Bot finishes |\n| **9 Ch3** | Escort, tide, Flare, Bloats, Bell-Hermit, Harpoon | Bot finishes |\n| **10 Ch5** | Lighthouse, Bailiffs, `quay_night`, Underwriter, cannon, escape, ending, credits | **Whole-game test passes** (Ch4 absent) |\n| **11 Ch4** | Rifle, Overwatch, bridge, funicular | Whole-game test still passes |\n| **12 Finish** | Attract loop complete, all music and barks, notes, Tin Gulls, Exclusives, Actuary, DESIGNERS.md, About pages from real answers, exit interview, final packaging | `tools/check` all green; §19 walked line by line |\n\n**If you run short, cut in this order and nothing else:**\n1. Tin Gulls and Exclusives.\n2. Ch4's Overwatch.\n3. Ch4 entirely (add the Seal Rifle to the Ch3 trader, and go by tunnel to the lighthouse with Mrs. Vane captured there).\n4. Actuary and costumes.\n\n**Never cut:** attract, dev mode, hub passing, settings, glyphs, touch-only screen, About, the Flenser, the Bell-Hermit, the Underwriter, the foghorn walk.\n\nYour brief's \"Done\" rule stands: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. If something's cut, it's gone from menus, code paths and text, not greyed out.\n\n---\n\n## 19. Delivery and full brief coverage\n\n**Package:** `tools/package` runs `build-web.sh --single-file --scene tide --title \"<title>\" ...` with `--out` pointing at the deliverable path your TASK.md names. Then run `tools/check`. When done, delete `engine/target` and any `node_modules` (2 GB+, rebuildable). Keep source. Keep all files inside your dev folder and the folder root your TASK.md gives, not `/tmp`. Stop only processes you started, by PID.\n\n**Engine feedback notes:** keep a short running list as you go, since your TASK.md asks what you changed and where you got stuck. §14.1 is most of it.\n\n**Final reply:** put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply as well as on the About screen. Further research is your choice. Report what you actually did, adding that this plan's research covered the engine source and the hub protocol.\n\n**Exit interview:** fill in the exit-interview file your TASK.md describes, with your own answers, and check it parses as JSON. Catalogue values for this game: type Game; genre Horror; source Resident Evil 4; series Resident Evil; players 1–4; tags such as `3d`, `third-person`, `co-op`, `horror`, `story`, `boss fights`.\n\n| Brief asks for | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Original game inspired by the source; world, characters, themes, tone turned into mechanics | §1, §2, §5 to §10 |\n| Genre and perspective chosen | §1 |\n| Title: riff, picked with a real RNG from 50 | Yours; intro of this plan |\n| Single HTML package | §3, §19 |\n| Dev subfolder; don't read outside; port and process rules | §3, §17, §19 |\n| Build on the shardfall engine, change anything | §3, §14.1, §16 |\n| Native art style as base, new art for the source's feel, library for generics | §14 |\n| Native animation as base, new animations | §14.4 |\n| All audio in code, gibberish voices, music 10% default | §15, §12.4, §17 |\n| Online: hub integration and game on its own | §11, §17 |\n| Performance budget unlimited, no optimization | §14.3 |\n| Headless tests, one command, failures and one-line count, whole-game playthrough, few screenshots, no review subagents | §17 |\n| Feature-complete vertical slice, long enough to show everything, what you can and can't do | §1, §4.3, §7 |\n| Infrastructure for later content with designer tools | §16.3 |\n| Dev mode from pause, standard tools, live sliders, reset | §13.2 |\n| Attract: 10 s idle, looping, AI-played, cheats allowed, any input exits | §13.1 |\n| Multiplayer | §11 |\n| Narrative style like the source's | §10 |\n| Controller-first 10-foot; DualSense standard mapping; native KB and mouse; mouse clicks menu items and world things; hover moves focus | §4.1, §12, §9 |\n| Prompts follow last input; PS glyphs, Xbox option in Settings; keys and mouse | §12.2 |\n| No dense web-style screens | §12.1 |\n| Touch-only: message, settings button, attract runs, no touch controls | §12.5 |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §18 |\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine, Prompt Feedback, in chat reply and in-game About | §13.3 |\n| Exit interview file | §19 |\n","numLines":301,"startLine":659,"totalLines":959}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019cPfKEY1dYebswtKnyN2nu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
